+  "body": "## Summary\n\nPushes the next two **v5-exclusive** RTE-TRUTH security residual packets onto the series branch `claude/rte-audit-improvement-f4beb7` (same vehicle as closed #1043).\n\n### TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009 \u2014 F-30 residuals\n- Neutralize literal `</repo_content>` in untrusted bodies before wrap (tag-break escape)\n- Route `rte_ops_surfaces` cost-preview through `build_extraction_prompt_prefix`\n- Frame `llm_runtime` comparison lane with `UNTRUSTED_CONTENT_PREAMBLE`\n- Package-wide (non-legacy) single-literal preamble guard + **wiring pins** (R3-008 vacuous-test lesson)\n\n### TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010 \u2014 F-23 residuals\n- Expand sensitive-key fragments: `credential`, `passwd`, `access_key` (reject bare `cred`/`auth`)\n- **Document** short free-text secret residual honestly \u2014 do not claim structural impossibility\n- Security scrub on **raw/** partition payloads and **partX** shards (R3-007 only covered norm/)\n- Unify redaction token to `[REDACTED]` across prompts and scrub\n\n### Commits (tip)\n- `d0e9fd7ae7` fix(rte): TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009 \u2014 delimiter escape + preamble unification\n- `0181fc9e8b` fix(rte): TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010 \u2014 close F-23 residuals (raw, short secrets, token)\n\nAlso includes prior series work (R3-001\u2026R3-008, R1, packets, etc.) on this branch.\n\n## Proof\n- `proof/rte-truth-program/TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009/PROOF.json`\n- `proof/rte-truth-program/TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010/PROOF.json`\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pytest services/repo-truth-extractor/tests/test_untrusted_content_delimiter.py`\n- [x] `pytest \u2026 -k 'delimiter or untrusted or preamble or comparison'`\n- [x] `pytest services/repo-truth-extractor/tests/test_write_time_secret_scrub.py`\n- [x] `pytest \u2026 test_secrets_redaction_binding.py test_output_safety.py`\n- [x] Mutation: identity neutralize reopens tag-break escape\n- [x] Mutation: disable raw partition scrub reopens bare-secret leak on raw/\n- [ ] CI on this PR\n\n## Notes / residuals\n- v5 exclusive (v3/v4 out of R3 scope; D-tier owns ports)\n- Short free-text secrets without key name or provider prefix remain **accepted residual**\n- ProcessPool worker `_op_write_json` still bypasses `write_json()` \u2014 pre-existing, not claimed closed",
