+      "messageBody": "## Packet 4 \u2014 generic project-control exporter\n(`TP-DMX-PCP-CORE-GENERIC-EXPORTER-0001`)\n\nFirst **runtime-code** packet. A read-only `pcp export` that inspects\nany Git repository and emits a `project_evidence_export` JSON validating\nagainst the **de-Dopemux'd** core schema \u2014 with **no named-system\ndependency**.\n\n> **Stacked on #944 (Packet 3).** Base is the P3 branch until #944\nmerges to main, then I'll re-target this PR to `main` (clean \u2014 P4 is all\nnet-new files).\n\n### What it does\n- `src/dopemux/pcp/{exporter,cli}.py` \u2014 `export_evidence(repo_path)`\ndiscovers repo root, real `head_sha` (40/64-hex), branch\n(detached\u2192null), dirty state; emits `generated_from_fixture=false` +\nreal `head_sha` (satisfies P3's runtime gate), all named-system sections\n`ABSENT`/`UNKNOWN` (fail-closed), `forbidden_action_confirmation` all\nfalse. **Self-validates** its output against the schema before\nreturning. `click` CLI (`python -m dopemux.pcp.cli export`).\n- **Read-only**: no writes, no network, no repo mutation.\n\n### Hardening (external PAL `gpt-5.2` review \u2192 PASS_WITH_RISKS, all 3\napplied)\n- Sanitized git env (strip `GIT_*`, `--no-pager`,\n`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, `-c\ncore.fsmonitor=false`) so a hostile repo config can't make git spawn an\nexternal helper.\n- NUL (`-z`) dirty-path parsing (correct for renames/quoted/spaced\npaths).\n- Accept SHA-1 **and** SHA-256 head_sha.\n\n### Validation\n**113 pytest pass** (12 new + 101 existing, no regressions); output\nself-validates; `export --help` works; pre-commit green.\n\nDraft / NEEDS_SUPERVISOR. Depends on Packet 3 (#944).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
