+      "messageBody": "\u2026outes\n\nPR Steward MUST_FIX Item 1 from #931 was the one of seven not carried into\nthe canonical #953/#954 OpenClaw DCP routing contracts. The top-level\nopenrouter_profile allowed null, and the only enforcement of a named profile\nwas keyed on provider == \"openrouter\". A SELECTED decision with\naccess_path == \"openrouter_paid\" but provider set to any other value (e.g.\n\"openai\", \"unknown\") could therefore carry openrouter_profile: null and\nbypass every per-profile allowlist \u2014 even though openclaw_dcp_routing_policy.yaml\nrequires openrouter_profile evidence for OpenRouter routes.\n\nAdd an allOf conditional to route_decision.schema.json requiring a named\n(non-null) openrouter_profile whenever decision_status == \"SELECTED\" AND\naccess_path == \"openrouter_paid\", bound to the six named profiles. The guard\nkeys on access_path (the routing plane), so it holds regardless of provider.\n\nAdd a negative regression test: SELECTED + openrouter_paid + null profile must\nfail for provider in {openrouter, openai, unknown}; the named-profile baseline\nand all R0-R6 + UNKNOWN example decisions still validate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
