+      "messageBody": "\u2026p binding\n\nPorts #975's net-new A1 activation layer onto the surgical stack, reconciled onto\n#978 wheel-safe schema loading (drops #975's competing _load_validator dual-path).\n\nTwo fail-closed gates run in route_mutation ONLY when execute is True AND a writer\nis registered (inert behaviour unchanged \u2014 no writer \u21d2 gates never fire):\n  - 6b assertion verification: default NoTrustedIssuerVerifier rejects\n    (ASSERTION_ISSUER_UNTRUSTED); a real signed-issuer verifier is injected at\n    activation. Verifier exceptions fail closed.\n  - 6c authority-map binding: default FailClosedAuthorityBinding rejects\n    (AUTHORITY_MAP_ABSENT); binding_from_entries requires a SOURCE entry with\n    live_write_allowed=true + BLOCK_OR_ESCALATE. The DCP map has no SOURCE entries\n    by design, so live writes stay impossible there.\n\nroute_mutation / create_bridge_router / create_bridge_app gain assertion_verifier +\nauthority_binding params (default None \u21d2 fail-closed defaults). New modules:\nassertion_auth.py, authority_binding.py.\n\nTests (grok's reconcile, validated against this port): LIVE-path tests inject a\npass-verifier + binding_from_entries; new gate tests; inert-CLI tests. Full\ntests/project_control_plane green incl. #978 parity + Red Line #15 guard.\n\nDeferred (additive, not load-bearing for the fail-closed default): optional\nissuer/signature fields on live_write_ready.schema.json for real signed assertions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
