+      "committedDate": "2026-07-27T03:01:50Z",
+      "messageBody": "\u2026 wiring\n\nCloses F-23 (CRIT, security; the second of PR #1043's two merge gates \u2014 F-30\nlanded in 27b349dd3), plus F-31, F-27 (H/M part), F-33 and F-08.\n\nF-23 \u2014 C8's SECRETS_RISK_LOCATIONS contract requires an *exact* <=200-char\nexcerpt, so every hardcoded_secret / secret_in_url / weak_credential finding\ncopied the real credential verbatim into the norm artifact AND into paid-LLM\ncontext, then fed R11 security synthesis. H1's redaction rule existed only\ninside the \"Legacy Context (for intent only; never as evidence)\" block \u2014\nexplicitly non-binding, and inert besides: the runtime injects no block by that\nname (documented at run_extraction_v4.py:104-110).\n\n  - PROMPTSET_RULES.md gains a binding \"## Secret Redaction Rules\" section that\n    explicitly OVERRIDES the exact-excerpt Evidence Rule where they conflict,\n    names the concrete <REDACTED> token, and shows five worked transforms\n    (AWS/OpenAI/Bearer-JWT/webhook-URL/PEM). Resolving the contradiction matters\n    as much as stating the rule: a model following the Evidence Rules literally\n    still emits the secret.\n  - C8 gains a binding SECRETS Hard Requirement + a redacted worked example (a\n    few-shot example carrying a live-looking secret teaches the opposite of the\n    rule). H1's redaction is promoted out of Legacy Context into the binding\n    body. H7 and the M3/M4/M5 safe-exports get binding rules too \u2014 M's vague\n    \"redact if found\" is what the audit flagged as insufficient.\n  - This reaches the model, not just the file: all six prompts point at\n    PROMPTSET_RULES.md via \"## Shared Rules\", and _inject_promptset_rules()\n    appends it before dispatch. A test asserts the *rendered* prompt for each of\n    the six contains the rules and the worked example.\n\nF-31 \u2014 required_prompt_sections had zero runtime readers; the section validator\nin template_renderer.py was wired to nothing, so a prompt could lose its\nAnti-Fabrication Rules and still run against a paid model. load_promptset() now\nenforces the contract and fails closed; the validator learns the promptset's\ndeclared sections and honors the \"## Shared Rules\" pointer, matching the offline\nlinter's semantics so runtime and lint agree. The shipped promptset yields 0\nissues across all 136 prompts \u2014 enforcement is live and blocks nothing real.\n\nAlso fixes a gap found while tracing F-31, not in the audit text: only the sync\ndispatch site injected the rules. The async R batch seam (v5 ~20196) read the\nprompt and submitted it with the Shared Rules pointer UNRESOLVED \u2014 the entire\nanti-fab regime, and now the redaction rule, never arrived on that path. Both\ncall sites are pinned by test.\n\nF-27 (H/M) / F-33 \u2014 stripped 21 generated_at lines across 17 A/H prompts whose\nGen-1 legacy shapes contradicted the binding Determinism Rules. Each removal was\nverified to lie inside a Legacy Context block first; no binding-body occurrence\nwas touched. T-phase is R3-005c's and is excluded from the regression test so it\ncannot fail on unlanded work. (Grep, not the finding text, is the authority: only\ngenerated_at was present \u2014 no run_id, and M-phase had none.)\n\nF-08 \u2014 three contract-map guards called pytest.skip() when their target vanished,\nreporting green while checking nothing. Now pytest.fail(). 23 pass / 0 skip: the\ntargets do emit, so this closes a latent hole rather than papering over a live one.\n\nValidation (dry-run only; no --execute, no DPMX_LIVE_OK, no live calls):\n  - new tests: 11 redaction + 6 section-enforcement + 130 determinism-key \u2014 all\n    mutation-verified. Removing each fix fails its tests (8+/11, 6/6, and many\n    parametrized cases respectively); the async-path test fails \"assert 1 == 2\",\n    reproducing the F-31 gap directly.\n  - packet verify -k 'promptset or redact or section': 105 passed\n  - goldens: 27 passed + 1 skip \u2014 NO GOLDEN MOVED (regeneration was\n    pre-authorized; empirically none was needed \u2014 verified, not assumed)\n  - promptset v4 linter: 10 passed, status PASS\n  - full suite: 1432 passed, 6 xfailed, 2 skipped, 1 failed \u2014\n    test_prescan_e2e_smoke, known pre-existing (tree-sitter degraded)\n  - NOT_RUN: the slow cost_preview golden hits its own 420s subprocess cap on\n    this machine; proven pre-existing by re-running it at clean HEAD with all\n    changes stashed. PAL chain NOT_RUN (no PAL in session) \u2014 no independent\n    review yet.\n\nResidual risk, stated plainly: this proves the redaction rule is binding, is\npresent, and reaches the assembled payload on both dispatch paths. It does NOT\nprove a live model obeys it \u2014 that needs live evals. The rule is an instruction,\nnot an enforcement; nothing re-scans the artifact at write time. The top\nfollow-up is a write-time scrub via output_safety.sanitize_payload_for_output(),\nwhich is what would make leakage structurally impossible. Flagged rather than\nsilently half-attempted.\n\nProof: proof/rte-truth-program/TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-004/PROOF.json\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
