+      "messageBody": "Adds a routing block per packet keyed to the canonical six-stage vocabulary\nin config/ai/model-routing.policy.yaml (advisory governance, not a runtime\nrouter \u2014 runtime wins on conflict).\n\nEach packet declares stage, tier, preferred/acceptable/forbidden runners,\nand a per-runner model id. Model ids are OBSERVED from this machine:\n  codex     gpt-5.6-sol / xhigh        (~/.codex/config.toml)\n  opencode  claude-sonnet-4-5 + haiku  (~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc)\n  grok      grok-code-fast-1 / high    (~/.grok/config.toml)\n  copilot   Claude Sonnet 4.5          (.github/agents/*.agent.md)\n  claude_code  Opus 5 / Sonnet 5 / Haiku 4.5\nBeyond these files, selector-string validity stays VERIFY_WITH_VENDOR_DOCS.\n\nTiers: 20 strong, 19 balanced, 6 cheap. Existing execution.recommended_model\n(luna/terra/sol, written by Codex) is preserved and maps 1:1 onto the tiers.\n\nTwo hard constraints encoded:\n  REVIEW-001 forbids claude_code \u2014 it authored R3-002/004/007 and the R1\n    seams, so it cannot audit itself (independent_audit_before_readiness)\n  D-003 forbids every autonomous runner \u2014 live paid dispatch, operator only\ngrok is forbidden as sole author at strong tier (fast coding tier, not\nstrong-reasoning); acceptable as implementer under an approved plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
