+      "messageBody": "\u2026ng 7 real defects\n\nR0-004's first config set `select = []`, so `ruff check` reported\n'All checks passed!' against zero enabled rules. Green badge, no signal \u2014\nthe same vacuous-pass shape as the prescan XPASS earlier on this branch.\n\nEnabling pyflakes surfaced 7 genuine defects, all fixed here:\n\n  F821 undefined-name x5\n    benchmarking/executors/prescan_adapter.py, and the three\n    benchmarking/validators/*_wrapper.py files, annotate with `Any`\n    without importing it; fl_int/reduce_input.py:242 uses `Optional`\n    without importing it. Latent rather than live only because each file\n    carries `from __future__ import annotations` \u2014 they become real\n    NameErrors the moment that import is dropped, and they already break\n    get_type_hints/mypy.\n\n  F811 redefined-while-unused x2\n    lib/prescan/engine.py imported PRESCAN_ARTIFACT_VERSION from\n    intelligence_router and then shadowed it with a hardcoded '1.0'.\n    Both values agree today, so it is benign \u2014 but bumping the canonical\n    constant would leave engine.py stamping the stale version and\n    silently violating SUPPORTED_PRESCAN_ARTIFACT_VERSIONS. Removed the\n    shadow, kept the import. Also dropped a duplicate aliased import in\n    run_extraction_v5.py.\n\nConfig now selects F and ignores only the high-count cosmetic members\n(F401/F841/F541), which need a 23k-line cleanup that belongs to a\nrefactor packet. Everything still enabled is a correctness signal.\n\nVerified non-vacuous: injecting an undefined name into a probe file\nproduces F821. Suite 1455 passed / 4 skipped / 6 xfailed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
