+      "messageBody": "\u2026mented values\n\nR3-005e retyped D3/E3/R5/X4 output contracts to `kind: json_graph` +\n`merge_strategy: graph_merge`. Neither value exists:\n\n  - zero occurrences of json_graph or graph_merge in runtime Python\n    (json_item_list appears 21 times)\n  - artifacts.yaml \u2014 the contract v4 actually reads \u2014 still declares\n    json_item_list / itemlist_by_id, so the prompts and the runtime\n    contract now disagreed. F-34 IS a prompt-vs-contract mismatch, so\n    this made the finding worse, not better.\n  - run_extraction_v4.py:579 only recognizes itemlist_by_id and\n    itemlist_by_service_id; graph_merge silently falls through to the\n    default merge, which is a BEHAVIOUR CHANGE, not a no-op.\n  - PROMPT_C16 already documents the ground truth in prose:\n    \"edges-as-items - no json_graph kind in runner\".\n\nR5 was additionally flipped from markdown/markdown_concat to a JSON\ngraph kind, which would misdeclare its output format outright.\n\nRestored all four to their original declared contracts. F-34 is NOT\nclosed: declaring a graph kind requires implementing json_graph and\ngraph_merge in the runner and artifacts.yaml FIRST - that is a runtime\npacket, not a prompt text edit.\n\nR3-005e's F-35 step renumbering and F-49 W/X/Z nits are correct and kept.\nPromptset suite green (40 passed).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
