+      "committedDate": "2026-07-27T08:43:10Z",
+      "messageBody": "\u2026 catalog\n\nF-10 (CRIT): lib/spend_ledger.py kept its own hardcoded $0.15/$0.60 baseline\nregistry that silently survived any catalog load failure while still\nreporting match_type=exact/unknown_model=False \u2014 a 33-50x under-price\npresented with full confidence. F-11 (CRIT): the preview/preventive path\n(E2, multiplier-adjusted) and the abort authority (E3, flat) priced identical\nusage differently, ~2x on flex-tier profiles, with both trackers able to\nindependently abort a run.\n\nextractor/costing.py is now the single pricing authority: load_pricing_registry\nreads config/pricing.yaml directly and raises on any problem (never a silent\nfallback); resolve_model_rate is the one candidate-matching lookup; compute_\noptimized_cost / estimate_usage_cost_usd apply the same optimizer multipliers\nin both E2 and E3. lib/spend_ledger.py is now a thin fa\u00e7ade that delegates to\nit and raises when an unknown model is priced with a spend cap set (mirrors\nE3's existing behavior), marking UNPRICED at $0.00 \u2014 never a fabricated\nnumber \u2014 when no cap is set. lib/prescan/cost_estimator.py gets the same\nfail-closed/UNPRICED treatment instead of swallowing catalog failures.\n\nAdded a coverage gate (tests/test_pricing_coverage_gate.py) tying every\nCOST_PROFILES route (cell_aliases + hardcoded ladder fallbacks) to a priced\nconfig/pricing.yaml row; it found and drove the fix for 5 real gaps\n(openrouter/openai/gpt-5.2-chat, gpt-5.2-pro, gpt-5-pro, gpt-4.1-nano,\ngpt-4o-mini), now priced at LOW/MEDIUM confidence with explicit caveats.\n\ntests/test_pricing_authority_unification.py is the core fixture-table proof\n(A2 \u00a75.5): preview, preventive check, and both E2/E3 accounting produce the\nsame dollar figure for identical usage across 5 scenarios including the\naudit-named flex-tier case, verified against the real config/pricing.yaml.\nCatalog-failure and unknown-model+cap raises are asserted at every entry\npoint and confirmed by mutation checks (guards temporarily disabled, tests\nwent red, then reverted clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
