+      "messageBody": "\u2026ture flag\n\nF-13 (MED): extractor.costing.record_request_cost priced a call, added its\ncost to total_cost_usd, appended the ledger entry, and only THEN compared\nagainst max_cost_usd -- a single over-cap call was fully committed to the\ndurable spend ledger before the breach was noticed (A2-7 one-call\novershoot). The cap check now runs on the projected total BEFORE any\ncommit: a breaching call's cost is never added to total_cost_usd and no\nledger entry is written for it. cost_cap_mode (declared \"preventive\" on\nevery shipped cost profile but consumed nowhere) is now wired to real,\nopposite, tested behavior: \"preventive\" (default) is the new pre-check\npath; \"post_hoc\" reproduces the exact pre-fix commit-then-compare overshoot\nas an explicit, opt-in-only legacy mode. make_projected_cost_check was\nverified dead in v5 (zero callers; it's a different, pre-dispatch E2\nmechanism) and left untouched rather than force-wired into an unrelated\nE3 fix.\n\nF-15 (MED): the spend ledger snapshot (SPEND_LEDGER.json, the money log)\nwas written via a full path.write_text() rewrite on every cost event --\na crash mid-write could truncate the only durable record of actual spend.\nNew write_json_atomic() writes to a temp file in the same directory then\nos.replace()s it into place; CostingDeps.write_json for the spend ledger\nnow points at it. Other write_json callers (partition artifacts,\ntelemetry, manifests) are unchanged -- this is scoped to the money log\nper the packet's mandate, not a blanket I/O rewrite.\n\nF-38/A2-8 (MED/LOW): sampling temperature was hardcoded 0.1 at three sites,\nwith no operator control, and only build_chat_payload's resolve_temperature\ncall honored the rule that OpenAI gpt-5* models must never receive a\ntemperature parameter at all (they reject it outright). New\n--llm-temperature flag (range-validated 0.0-2.0 at both the dopemux click\nlayer and v5's own argparse layer, default 0.1) threads through\nRunnerConfig.llm_temperature into build_chat_payload and llm_runtime's\nGemini-native config dict. resolve_temperature remains the single\nomission-policy choke point -- gpt-5 models still receive no temperature\nkey regardless of what an operator requests, proven by a mutation-checked\ntest across five different requested values.\n\nEvery fix has a mutation-checked test: each was reverted in isolation and\nconfirmed to fail its corresponding test before being restored. Golden\nharness stays green (help_rte_run intentionally regenerated for the new\nflag's --help text; the slow cost-preview golden shows zero dollar drift).\nFull service suite (~1300+ tests) green. Dry-run only throughout; no\n--execute, no DPMX_LIVE_OK, no live provider calls.\n\nextractor/cli_args.py and src/dopemux/cli.py are outside this packet's\nliteral (pre-R1-002) file-boundary list but were necessarily touched: v5's\nargparse definitions -- including the precedent --max-cost-usd flag --\nalready live in cli_args.py post-seam-extraction, and dopemux rte run is\nthe documented canonical operator entrypoint. Both are called out\nexplicitly in PROOF.json rather than silently done.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
