+      "messageBody": "R2-004 fixed F-19d in RUN_MANIFEST but the same class of leak survived one\nfunction away: print_config (run_extraction_v5.py:19012) emitted the raw\nDPMX_WEBHOOK_URL value on every --print-config, while the webhook SECRET\ndirectly beside it was already correctly reported as a boolean.\n\nThe URL is a capability URL - possession of it is authorization - so\nprinting it to stdout put it in terminal scrollback and CI logs. The\nR2-004 agent flagged this as out of its file boundary rather than\nsilently widening scope, which was the right call; fixing it here.\n\nNow reports presence only (dpmx_webhook_url_set), matching\ndpmx_webhook_secret_set.\n\nCommitted goldens were NOT exposed: the P0 harness normalizer already\nmasks dpmx_webhook_* (tests/goldens/_normalize.py:124), so they stored\n\"<MASKED>\". Verified before assuming.\n\nGoldens regenerated deliberately; diff is exactly the key rename across\n13 files (24 insertions / 24 deletions, sole content change\ndpmx_webhook_url -> dpmx_webhook_url_set). Suite 1496 passed / 4 skipped\n/ 6 xfailed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
