+      "committedDate": "2026-07-27T19:21:36Z",
+      "messageBody": "\u2026alidating defects\n\nAdds scripts/check_workflow_syntax.py and wires it as a pre-commit hook.\n\nThis guard deliberately does NOT run in CI. Both defect classes it detects\nmake GitHub reject the workflow file at parse time, so zero jobs run and any\nCI-side check is never reached \u2014 a CI job cannot catch a defect that stops CI\nfrom starting. That is exactly how F-55 survived on PR #1136: the check list\nlooked largely green while all 14 required gates were absent, not failing.\n\nDetects:\n  EXPR-ESCAPE \u2014 backslash-escaped quote inside a ${{ }} expression. Actions\n    escapes an embedded quote by doubling it (''); a backslash invalidates the\n    entire file. Arises when shell escaping leaks out of a heredoc.\n  ORPHAN-ARG  \u2014 a `--flag` line inside a `run:` block scalar whose predecessor\n    lacks a trailing backslash, so the shell runs the flags as their own\n    command (exit 127 under `bash -e`) and they never reach the intended one.\n\nNeither is detectable by grepping for inserted text \u2014 the very check that let\nboth defects through.\n\nMutation-verified rather than asserted:\n  1. clean ci-complete.yml            -> PASS (exit 0)\n  2. F-55 reinjected in isolation     -> EXPR-ESCAPE at :629, exit 1\n  3. F-56 reinjected in isolation     -> ORPHAN-ARG  at :347, exit 1\n  4. all 17 real workflow files       -> PASS (exit 0)\n  5. pre-commit run --all-files       -> Passed\nMutations were applied to scratchpad copies; the repo files were untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
