+      "committedDate": "2026-07-27T19:28:44Z",
+      "messageBody": "\u2026ion site\n\nF-42: most Repo Truth Extractor subcommands were DEFINED on the `upgrades`\ngroup and merely aliased onto `rte`, inverting the intended relationship \u2014\n`rte` is the surface the docs, wizard and quickstart all steer users to.\n\nInverted: the decorators now target `rte`, `upgrades` is marked hidden and\ncarries a deprecation notice on invoke, and the same Command/Group objects\nare registered back onto `upgrades` so every path historically reachable as\n`dopemux upgrades <x>` keeps working. Click commands carry no parent pointer,\nso multi-group registration is safe and was already used elsewhere here.\n\nAlso removes a genuine duplicate: there were TWO `promptset` groups \u2014 one on\n`upgrades` carrying only `audit`, one on `rte` carrying `audit`/`sync`/\n`validate`. Collapsed to the canonical `rte` group. NOTE this widens\n`upgrades promptset` to include `sync` and `validate`, which it never had.\nThe widening is additive (nothing removed), matches the A4 audit spec, and is\ncalled out here rather than buried because it exceeds pure alias preservation.\n\nBackward compatibility is proven by enumeration, not sampling: the parity test\niterates the live `upgrades.commands` registry, asserts nothing pre-existing\ndisappeared, asserts the alias set is a subset of the canonical set, and\nasserts each alias entry IS the same object as its canonical counterpart \u2014\nrecursing into the promptset subgroup. `scan` and `wizard` remain correctly\ncanonical-only; they were never reachable under `upgrades`.\n\nVerification (mutation-checked by execution, not asserted):\n  - remove \"trace\" from the alias loop -> parity test RED on the\n    nothing-disappeared assertion; pre-existing trace test also RED.\n  - alias `promptset` to a different Group object -> parity test RED:\n    \"`upgrades promptset` is not the same object as `rte promptset`\".\n  - revert cli.py entirely -> all four new tests RED, so none is vacuous.\n  - tests/unit/test_cli_upgrades_commands.py: 27/27 pass (23 pre-existing + 4).\n  - Golden harness: zero goldens moved (no golden references `upgrades`).\n  - End-to-end via the real CLI: `upgrades` absent from top-level help, `rte`\n    present, `upgrades --help` exit 0, deprecation surfaced on invoke,\n    upgrades \u2286 rte with every shared entry object-identical.\n\nThe implementing agent identified that one of its own tests was vacuous \u2014 the\n\"rte does not leak the deprecation warning\" case passes trivially pre-fix \u2014\nand re-grounded it by injecting the warning into the `rte` callback instead.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
