+      "messageBody": "\u2026 not dead\n\nF-07 listed three \"trivial dead-code deletions\". Two were genuinely dead. The\nthird was not \u2014 it was silently paying for duplicate LLM ingestion.\n\n1. extractor/phases/a.py \u2014 \"compose.yml\" appeared TWICE in phase A's `targets`.\n   Not cosmetic. `targets` flows to `Collector.collect(subdirs=targets)`, which\n   builds `roots = [self.root / d for d in subdirs]` and, when a root is a file,\n   appends `_make_item(root)` with no de-duplication anywhere in the method.\n   Proven empirically against the real Collector on a temp repo:\n       subdirs=[\"compose.yml\"]                -> 1 item\n       subdirs=[\"compose.yml\", \"compose.yml\"] -> 2 items\n   So every phase-A run collected compose.yml twice and shipped its content to\n   a paid model twice. Reclassifying this from \"trivial dead code\" to a real\n   wasted-spend defect.\n\n2. src/dopemux/ux/wizard/preflight.py:47 \u2014 `StageStatus.COMPLETED if all_ok\n   else StageStatus.COMPLETED`. Both branches identical. Stated once now.\n   `all_ok` is retained; it still selects the message. A failed system check is\n   deliberately a warning here, not a stage failure \u2014 noted in-line so this is\n   not later \"repaired\" into FAILED by accident.\n\n3. src/dopemux/ux/wizard/preflight.py:127 \u2014 `failures` scanned `checks` for a\n   failed \"Repository root\" entry, but that list is always empty at this point:\n   both sites that append a failed root return FAILED immediately (:72->:73 and\n   :75->:76), so control only reaches the tail once the root check passed. The\n   branch was unreachable, not a safety net. Verified by enumerating every\n   append site, not by inspection of the happy path alone.\n\nThe packet's third target, cli.py's `_add_extractor_alias_if_missing`, was\nalready removed by TP-RTE-TRUTH-R4-002 (34e3b3c6a2) \u2014 confirmed zero remaining\nreferences. No action needed; recorded so the packet is not re-opened.\n\nAdded tests/test_r0_007_phase_target_duplicates.py:\n  - parametrized over EVERY phase module, not just a.py, so the same defect in\n    a sibling phase is caught rather than only the instance F-07 named;\n  - a companion test pinning `Collector.collect()`'s non-dedup behaviour, so the\n    reason the first test exists cannot be forgotten. If collect() is ever made\n    to de-duplicate, that test fails and points back at this guard rather than\n    letting dedup silently mask a real list bug.\n\nVerification (run, not asserted):\n  - Reintroduced the duplicate -> RED: \"a.py repeats scan target(s)\n    ['compose.yml']\". Restored -> 6 passed.\n  - Golden harness: 27 passed, 1 skipped, zero goldens moved. Noted honestly:\n    NO golden covers phase A's target list, so the goldens are evidence for the\n    preflight.py changes only, not for item 1 \u2014 hence the direct Collector proof.\n  - Root wizard/preflight tests: 41 passed, 3 skipped (pre-existing quarantines).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
