+      "messageBody": "\u2026ynthesis-tier steps\n\nF-29. Synthesis-tier steps (R7, R8, S4, S5, S6) emitted claims with no way to\ntrace an individual claim back to the upstream artifact and item it came from.\nAdds a `## Synthesis Evidence Rules` section to PROMPTSET_RULES.md defining the\n{upstream_artifact, item_id, excerpt} citation shape \u2014 modelled on R11's\nexisting `<- ARTIFACT:item_id` convention rather than inventing a new one \u2014 and\npoints all five prompts at it.\n\nLANE (the distinction that matters here, since a contract that binds nowhere\nchanges nothing): this lands on the REQUEST-TIME path, not the offline one.\nrun_extraction_v5.py calls _inject_promptset_rules() at both dispatch sites\n(:13751 sync, :20505 async R-batch), and that function appends the whole of\nPROMPTSET_RULES.md to any prompt containing \"## Shared Rules\". Reviewer\nverified by executing the real function against the real R7 prompt file: the\ninjected text gains 8218 chars and contains \"Synthesis Evidence Rules\",\n\"upstream_artifact\", \"item_id\" and \"excerpt\". Not a document sitting unread.\n\nDeliberately NOT given a JSON output schema. All five steps emit kind: markdown\nartifacts, so lib/phase_contract_map.py never builds an OpenAI structured-output\nschema for them (it is scope: \"json_managed_only\"). The model prompt this\nfinding points at, R11, is likewise markdown-only and textual-contract-only.\nInventing a JSON schema here would be exactly the unimplemented-value mistake\nthat forced R3-005e's revert. The agent checked and declined; recorded rather\nthan quietly worked around.\n\nEnforcement is offline-lint only, and labelled as such: _synthesis_evidence_issues()\nin scripts/repo_truth_extractor_promptset_audit_v4.py runs from run_audit() via\ntests and manual --strict CLI runs, never on the dispatch path \u2014 the same status\nas its sibling checks in that file.\n\nALLOWLIST EXTENSION, approved and stated rather than silently taken: the packet\nallows promptsets/v4/ and services tests, but the lint machinery lives only at\nrepo-root scripts/, and the already-in-allowlist tests/test_promptset_v4_lint.py\nimports it directly. Validator work for this finding is structurally forced\noutside the declared allowlist. The agent flagged it instead of expanding scope\nquietly.\n\nVerification (run, not asserted): reverting the 5 prompts + PROMPTSET_RULES.md\nturns the lint test RED with all 6 expected issues; reverting PROMPTSET_RULES.md\nalone turns both injection tests RED; commenting out the run_audit() wiring line\nturns the wiring test RED; stubbing _synthesis_evidence_issues() to return []\nturns the two negative tests RED. Goldens: 27 passed, 1 skipped, zero moved.\n\nThe agent reported honestly that three positive tests are mutation-insensitive\nto the return-[] stub (they assert issues == [], which a no-op satisfies), and\nmarked two further tests NOT_RUN as distinct mutations rather than implying\ncoverage it had not exercised.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
