+      "messageBody": "\u2026es the run it reports\n\nBare `dopemux rte status` (no --run-id) minted a NEW timestamped run id on every\ninvocation, materialised its directory, and then reported THAT run \u2014 every phase\nNOT_STARTED, all counters 0. An operator checking a real extraction was shown a\nconfident, well-formatted report of a run that never happened, while the real\nrun's status was never surfaced. Truthfulness defect, not a stray write.\n\nTwo independent causes, both fixed:\n  1. run-id resolution: resolve_run_context() consulted the latest-run file only\n     in its `elif resume_requested:` branch; with no --run-id and no --resume it\n     fell through to generate_run_id() even under readonly. Adds\n     _resolve_latest_run_id() plus a `resolve_latest_when_readonly` parameter,\n     and refactors the --resume branch onto the shared helper.\n  2. the write: extractor/ui.py's UI._emit_event appended to\n     telemetry/TERMINAL_TIMELINE.jsonl under run_root, and that append mkdir'd\n     the parent \u2014 so the run dir appeared even on the readonly path. UI now\n     takes readonly and _emit_event no-ops when set.\n\nDESIGN NOTE \u2014 the naive fix was rejected deliberately. `readonly_introspection`\nalso covers --print-config, --print-run-order and friends, which legitimately\nneed NO existing run and ARE captured in goldens. Making all readonly paths\nrequire a run would break --print-config on a fresh repo. So this introduces a\nNARROWER `readonly_run_report` (status/status_json/coverage_report/\nverify_phase_output/tail_run_log) \u2014 only commands that report ON a run resolve\none. Config-printing commands are untouched.\n\nReviewer-verified independently against the real CLI, all five criteria:\n  - bare `rte status`: exit 1, run-dir count unchanged 5 -> 5, message\n    \"No extraction run found (no .../latest_run_id.txt and no --run-id given).\n     Start a run first with `rte run ...`, or pass --run-id explicitly.\"\n  - `rte status --run-id run_20260710T213737Z`: exit 0, reports that run, no dir\n  - `rte list` (--print-config) with zero runs: exit 0, no dir created\n  - goldens: 27 passed, 1 skipped, zero moved\n  - F-59 tests in isolation (R2-005's hunks reverse-applied out): 54 passed\n\nAgent mutation check, run live: stashing the three source files reproduces the\nbug exactly \u2014 `run=run_20260727T202807Z ... NOT_STARTED=15` with the run and\ntelemetry dirs freshly created; restoring resolves the real run and creates no\ntelemetry dir.\n\nRetires the FA-7-MED-1 deferral: tests/regression/audit_2026_05_22/\ntest_fa_7_med_1_status_no_telemetry.py's strict xfail (\"--status writes\ntelemetry under a typo'd run-id ... xfail until --status wraps the telemetry\nwriter in readonly_introspection\") is removed, because that is precisely what\ncause 2 fixes. That test edit was authored by the concurrent R2-005 agent\nagainst this fix; verified above to pass with only this packet's hunks applied,\nso the retirement stands on this change alone.\n\nNOT DONE \u2014 the packet's Priority 2 (F-43/F-44) is untouched, reconnaissance\nonly: --workers/-w vs --partition-workers canonicalisation, routing-policy\nChoice de-duplication, wizard estimate rewiring to lib/pricing_surface (its\ncost_profiles.py is a static ROUTING_LADDERS snapshot \"last synced 2026-07-12\"),\nreconciling the three status implementations, `rte trace` live-mode disposition,\nand the scan phase list's missing S. Overlaps F-47/R4-006, since `extract\ntruth-run` is dead code (raises unconditionally above ~380 unreachable lines).\n\nRoot suite shows 21 failed / 3 errors, all in orchestrator, TUI, DCP, CI and\npr_merge_specialist paths with no overlap with this change \u2014 independently\nreported as pre-existing by the R4-002 agent, which reproduced them with its\nown changes stashed out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
