+      "messageBody": "\u2026ER-006 deferrals, relabel 3 honestly\n\nF-17: _build_optimize_payload() nested prior-pass results under synthetic\ndedup_results/discovery_results/feasibility_results wrapper keys, diverging from\nthe flat contract the other three _build_*_payload methods follow. Merged flat.\nReviewer verified the load-bearing claim independently: those three wrapper keys\nhave ZERO references anywhere in the repo outside the new docstring, so nothing\ndownstream (prompt, schema or consumer) ever read them. Retires the\ntest_prescan_contracts.py deferral, replacing it with two tests (flat shape, and\nstr-serialization before _call_grok).\n\nF-16: test_prescan_incremental.py's semantic-parity assertion failed on\nsource_identity.artifact_root, which differs by design because the test writes\nthe full and incremental runs to different output directories so the second does\nnot clobber the baseline it diffs against. Normalized alongside generated_at.\nReviewer verified this masks nothing: an independent probe diffing the raw\noutputs WITHOUT the normalization reports exactly one divergence \u2014\n\".../incremental_out\" vs \".../full_out\" \u2014 and nothing semantic. Deferral retired.\n\nF-19: RUN.log grew unbounded. configure_run_file_logger() now uses\nRotatingFileHandler (DPMX_RUN_LOG_MAX_BYTES, default 10 MiB; backups via\nDPMX_RUN_LOG_BACKUP_COUNT), with max_bytes=0 as an explicit opt-out falling back\nto the plain FileHandler. Verified wired, not merely imported.\n\nTHE THREE DARWIN XFAILS ARE NOT FIXED, AND ARE NOT CLAIMED FIXED. The\ntest_code_prescan_truthfulness.py triplet carried\nxfail(sys.platform == \"darwin\", reason=\"prescan schema/runtime drift\"). That\nreason is a false attribution: on a machine without tree-sitter (it lives in the\n`services` extra) CodePrescan runs degraded and returns imports/api_surfaces/\nsymbols empty unconditionally, so the assertions fail for a missing optional\ndependency, not for drift. The agent verified each one fails genuinely rather\nthan passing vacuously \u2014 and noted one half of one assertion holds only by\ncoincidence (expected [] and got []). Converted to\nskipif(not TREE_SITTER_AVAILABLE) with honest per-test reasons, matching the\nprecedent already set in test_prescan_e2e_smoke.py. TP-RTE-WALKER-006 stays OPEN\nfor these three.\n\nWorth recording: because the old condition was sys.platform == \"darwin\", these\nthree have been running as ORDINARY tests on linux CI all along \u2014 where\ntree-sitter is installed via --extra services \u2014 and CI is green. So they already\npass on a complete environment; the marker was masking a local dependency gap,\nnot a real defect, and it would also have let a genuine drift regression hide\nbehind a Mac-only marker.\n\nSuite: 1704 passed, 7 skipped, 0 xfailed (baseline 1686/4/6). Six deferrals\nresolved: 3 closed for real (this packet's two plus FA-7, fixed by R4-004), 3\nrelabelled and still open.\n\nNOT DONE, flagged rather than forced: F-19's retention half \u2014\nextraction_hygiene.run_scan/run_apply remain unwired from the live CLI. The only\nsafe integration point sat inside the arg-dispatch block another agent was\nediting uncommitted at the time, and run_scan does two full repo_root.rglob(\"*\")\nwalks with no existing coverage, so wiring it into --doctor's default path risks\nan untested performance regression on this monorepo.\n\nNote on shared files: run_extraction_v5.py carries hunks from two packets. This\ncommit contains only the log-rotation hunks (the logging.handlers import, the\nRUN_LOG_* constants, and configure_run_file_logger); the readonly/status hunks\nbelong to TP-RTE-TRUTH-R4-004 (ec34d2afd5) and were committed separately. The\nsplit was verified by reverse-applying each side and confirming the file still\ncompiles and the other packet's tests still pass alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
