+      "messageBody": "\u2026, H9 sha256, E-phase contracts\n\nF-21 / F-25 / F-37. Fourteen prompts asked the model for things it cannot\nhonestly produce, or pointed it at artifacts that do not exist.\n\nH9: HOMECTRL_NORM_MANIFEST required `sha256` from the model. An LLM cannot\ncompute a file digest, so requiring one invites fabrication \u2014 and the runtime\nalready computes real digests itself from actual file bytes\n(run_repscan.py:143). Dropped from required_item_fields; no sha256 reference\nremains in the prompt. Verified this creates no contract mismatch: artifacts.yaml\nrequires sha256 zero times anywhere.\n\nE-phase: E1-E6's step 1 told the model to load `EXEC_INVENTORY.json`, which is\nnot the real upstream artifact name. E5 and E6 also carried generic scaffold\nfield sets (`component`/`symbol`, `risk`/`location`) that did not match their own\nwell-written procedure text. Contracts realigned to the procedure:\n  EXEC_ARTIFACT_SURFACE: id, artifact_path, persistence_type, component_owner,\n                         path, line_range, evidence\n  EXEC_RISK_FACTS:       id, risk_type, severity, mitigation_evidence,\n                         path, line_range, evidence\nThis also closes a latent mismatch rather than creating one: artifacts.yaml\nrequires path/line_range/id for both, and the OLD EXEC_RISK_FACTS line\n(`id, risk, severity, location, evidence`) contained neither path nor\nline_range \u2014 so the runtime union forced the model to emit fields its own prompt\nnever demonstrated. That is the same C14-class defect R3-003 flagged; the new\nfield sets include all three.\n\nM-phase: M0-M6 instructed live SQLite/ConPort/MCP interrogation the extractor\ncannot perform. Recast to static-repo evidence with explicit UNKNOWN fallbacks\nrather than invention. M3/M4/M5 also had a hardcoded implementer model name\n(F-37) removed.\n\nDID NOT TOUCH the landmine, deliberately: PROMPT_E3 still declares\n`kind: json_item_list` / `merge_strategy: itemlist_by_id` against a\n`nodes, edges, schema` shape. That contradiction (F-8/F-34) is what the reverted\nR3-005e tried to fix by inventing `json_graph`/`graph_merge` \u2014 values no runtime\nrecognises, so run_extraction_v4.py silently fell through to a different merge.\nIt belongs to that packet's scope, not this one, and remains open.\n\nReviewer-verified independently: the diff changes ZERO `kind:` or\n`merge_strategy:` lines (grep count 0 across all touched files). Only\nrequired_item_fields, id_rule and prose changed. id_rule confirmed to have zero\nruntime readers. Mutation check on the most consequential change \u2014 restoring\n`sha256` to H9's required fields \u2014 turns\ntest_h9_homectrl_norm_manifest_no_longer_requires_sha256 and\ntest_h9_prompt_body_has_no_other_sha256_reference RED; restoring returns 42/42.\n\nThe agent achieved 100% mutation coverage: reverting the promptset directory\nturns ALL 42 new tests red, and it self-corrected an M6 phrasing that had\nfalse-positived its own assertion rather than weakening the test.\n\nLane: H9/E5/E6 required_item_fields bind at REQUEST TIME (parsed by\nlib/phase_contract_map.py, unioned in lib/structured_output_contracts.py:326,\nfeeding the OpenAI response_format schema). The M-phase and E1-E6 step-1 changes\nare model-facing prose with no parsed binding.\n\nSuite: 1746 passed, 7 skipped (baseline 1704/7) \u2014 delta exactly the 42 new tests.\nZero goldens moved.\n\nNoted, not fixed: eight other prompts (A0, A99, C8, M3, M4, S12, Z2, Z9) still\nrequest sha256; if H9's reasoning holds it likely applies to some of them.\nM1/M2 will now legitimately emit UNKNOWN-heavy output \u2014 the honest consequence\nof the recast, not a regression.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
