+      "messageBody": "\u2026y; record generated-promptset disposition\n\nF-47: extract_commands.truth_run raises click.ClickException unconditionally as\nthe first statement of its body, leaving the entire implementation below it\nunreachable \u2014 v3-migration copy logic, hygiene scan, cleanup phase, and the\nsubprocess.Popen launch. Removed. Unreachability was proven, not assumed: no\nif/try guards the raise, and the live CLI was invoked to observe it fire.\n\nDeleted 269 lines, not the packet's estimated ~380. The estimate over-counted by\nincluding three helpers that are not in fact dead \u2014 see below. Reporting the\nreal number rather than the estimate.\n\nAlso deleted _display_scan_results (38 lines), whose only call site was inside\nthe removed body and which has zero references anywhere \u2014 verified across .py,\n.md, .yaml, .yml and .json, with no __all__ export and no test import.\n\nTHREE ORPHANED HELPERS KEPT, AND THE REASON STATED PLAINLY: reviewer counts,\nindependently reproduced by the agent, are\n\n  _build_truth_run_command        prod callers 0   test refs 6\n  _find_runner                    prod callers 0   test refs 1\n  _display_v3_migration_summary   prod callers 0   test refs 3\n\nThey have NO production callers. They survive only because tests import and call\nthem directly \u2014 a test pinning an unreachable callee, which reads as coverage\nwhile verifying nothing reachable (test_truth_run_cli.py is the main site, and it\nsits in the extractor smoke CI gate). They are kept only because deleting them\nrequires editing test files outside this packet's allowlist, and legacy-surface\nretirement is its own wave (F-50 / R5-001). Recorded here so the next reader is\nnot misled by that coverage.\n\nRemoved the now-unused module imports shutil, subprocess and CalledProcessError,\nstranded by the deletion. Worth noting these would NOT have been caught by lint:\nthe service ruff config deliberately ignores F401. Verified unused by grep,\nthen by import and by running the affected tests.\n\nF-48 DECISION \u2014 annotate promptsets/generated/ as disposable and regenerate on\ndemand; do NOT add a CI drift gate. Recorded with evidence in a new\npromptsets/generated/README.md. The evidence, which drove the call:\n  - Zero runtime consumers: run_extraction_v5.py reads only from promptsets/v4/.\n  - Zero test consumers of the checked-in snapshot; test_universal_extractor.py\n    exercises run_sync against synthetic tmp_path fixtures.\n  - A regenerate-and-diff gate is structurally unworkable as things stand:\n    sync_engine._compute_repo_hash hashes the ABSOLUTE repo path, so\n    regenerating from a different worktree produces a different directory name\n    for the same repo. Demonstrated live, and the throwaway output removed.\n  - It is a scope mismatch, not drift: 5 base templates / 61 steps versus v4's\n    136 \u2014 a separate, less mature prototype rather than a stale mirror.\nA gate here would raise false drift alarms while protecting nothing real.\n\nNo mutation checks: this packet adds no tests (deletion plus documentation), so\nthere is nothing to mutate. Reported as NOT_RUN rather than dressed up.\n\nVerification: extract group still exposes cleanup/docs/pipeline/truth-run;\ndirectly affected tests 97 passed, 1 skipped; root suite 21 failed / 3 errors,\nmatching the pre-existing baseline exactly with nothing additional.\n\nFurther zero-referenced code found and left for the retirement wave rather than\nfolded in: _load_hygiene_module and _hygiene_severity_color (the latter already\ndead before this change), and test_phase_interaction.py::_load_extract_cmds,\nwhich searches for a marker comment that has never existed and is itself never\ncalled.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
