+      "messageBody": "Removes the duplicate/dead MCP fleet start scripts and legacy compose\noverlays identified by claudedocs/mcp-legacy-launch-path-worklist-2026-07-28.md,\nper the P-22 packet in claudedocs/mcp-fleet-multi-instance-design-2026-07-28.md \u00a79.\n\nDeleted (14 files covering all 15 worklist paths \u2014 docker/mcp-servers/ is a\ngit-tracked symlink to docker/mcp-servers-source/, so the two worklist\nentries for start-all-mcp-servers.sh under those paths are the same file):\n- scripts/start-all-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/manage-mcp-servers.sh, scripts/mcp/manage-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/install-docker-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/deploy/deployment/{start-all,start-mcp-servers,stack_up_all}.sh\n- scripts/memory/start-memory-stack.sh\n- scripts/setup.sh\n- compose/legacy/{conport-kg,leantime-overlay}-docker-compose.yml\n- docker/mcp-servers-source/{start-all-mcp-servers,start-profile,setup-task-orchestrator}.sh\n\nRuntime fixes required before these could safely go (discovered by tracing\nactual callers, not just grepping filenames):\n- src/dopemux/mcp/provision.py: MCPProvisioner used \"start-all-mcp-servers.sh\"\n  as its \"is this a valid MCP stack\" sentinel across every candidate source\n  (project local/source/vendor/cache/package template). Deleting the script\n  without changing this would have made `ensure_stack_present()` unlink the\n  docker/mcp-servers symlink and then raise, breaking `dopemux init`'s\n  MCP-provisioning flow. Swapped the sentinel to README.md, which ships with\n  every copy of the vendored tree and isn't a launch path.\n- src/dopemux/commands/mcp_commands.py: `dopemux mcp up` (no --repo) shelled\n  out to scripts/start-all-mcp-servers.sh directly for the --all/default\n  case. Replaced with the same docker-compose-service-list approach `mcp\n  down` already uses (DEFAULT_MCP_SERVICES \u2229 compose services), so `dopemux\n  mcp up --all` \u2014 the command INSTALL.md now documents as canonical \u2014 no\n  longer depends on a script that doesn't exist.\n- .claude/hooks/mcp_health_probe.py: generic remediation suggestion changed\n  from `docker compose up -d {name}` to `dopemux mcp up --services {name}`.\n- .vibe/config.toml: task-orchestrator entry repointed from the FastAPI\n  shadow-twin at :8000 to the canonical Kotlin jar singleton at\n  127.0.0.1:7890/mcp (streamable HTTP), per design migration step M10.\n\nReference updates: INSTALL.md (drops the raw-script alternative at\n~L1157, extends the compose-deprecation note to cover the removed\ncompose/legacy/ files), scripts/README.md, docs/03-reference/services/\nserver-registry{,-2}.md and the vendored SERVER_REGISTRY.md copy (Quick\nReference now points at `dopemux mcp up --all`), and\nscripts/deploy/setup/install-mcp-servers.sh's closing hints.\n\nAdded tests/mcp/test_no_legacy_fleet_start_paths.py: a CI guard that walks\ngit-tracked executable files (*.sh/*.py/*.ps1/Makefile \u2014 prose in docs/JSON\ncan't launch anything) for `docker compose up` / `docker-compose up` and\nfails on any hit outside an explicitly justified allowlist. The sweep\nsurfaced two pre-existing, out-of-worklist direct-compose paths (Makefile's\npm-up/webhook_receiver targets, docker/leantime/configure_bridge.sh, and an\nunscoped scripts/deploy/setup/setup_dopemux.sh with no live caller) that are\nallowlisted with a note flagging them for a follow-up packet rather than\nrewritten here, to keep this change to the safe subset.\n\nUpdated tests/mcp/test_provision.py, tests/test_cli_mcp_startup.py, and\ntests/test_mcp_health_probe.py for the sentinel/suggestion-string changes\nabove.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
