+      "messageBody": "Supervisor decision: GO with mandatory design corrections\n(GO_DRAFT_PR / GO_M0_ONLY / BLOCK_M1_M5_PENDING_PREREQUISITES).\n\n- D1 (10.1): Kotlin TO end-state = project-scoped leased-port instances\n  (one jar per project, new ADR required, packet P-24). Corrects the\n  'revert reason UNKNOWN' claim: PR #1086 was closed for bundling an\n  unapproved authority change - governance rejection, not technical\n  proof. multi_project_singleton stays NOT authorized; switch-project\n  is transitional only.\n- D2 (10.2): python :8000 service is RENAMED (candidate\n  dopemux-workflow-api), not retired - DopeconBridge and workflow/MCP\n  surfaces depend on it; M11 rewritten as bounded rename packet.\n- D3 (10.3): ConPort end-state = project-scoped, never host-singleton;\n  P-18/CRS v2 rewritten around a fixed project tenant with the wall in\n  storage; P-19 flip target corrected.\n- D4 (10.4): redis-events project-scoped NOW; P-21 elevated to P0 -\n  dope-memory promotes activity.events.v1 into work_log_entries via a\n  global consumer group, refuting the events-are-advisory premise.\n- Migration section records M0-only authorization; M10 marked executed.\n- AGENTS.md 12.6, .claude/claude.md, and 12 reader-facing docs updated\n  from 'pending retirement' to 'pending rename' and corrected end-states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
