+      "messageBody": "\u2026lback, M10 revert\n\nSupervisor verdict on PR #1150: NEEDS_REPAIR_BEFORE_READY. Three repairs:\n\n1. redis-events documentation no longer claims project-scoped as 'class\n   today'. AGENTS.md 12.6, .claude/claude.md, and design 1.2/5.1 now state\n   OBSERVED runtime = host singleton (unsafe/noncompliant for\n   multi-project), REQUIRED immediate target = project-scoped, gate =\n   P-21 implementation + isolation validation. The ruling changed the\n   authorized target, not the running container.\n\n2. Design M3 rewritten: BLOCKED with rollback UNKNOWN. M0 established\n   /private/tmp/pal-model-refresh no longer contains its compose file, so\n   the previously stated rollback was impossible. M3 stays blocked until\n   a bounded packet proves deterministic recreation (pinned ensure-pal.sh\n   revision, image digest, mounts/volumes/command/redacted env,\n   shadow-name recreation, health + Codex docker exec verification).\n\n3. .vibe/config.toml task-orchestrator entry REVERTED to :8000. Port 7890\n   is currently held by the dNh_CRM jar and switch-project does not exist\n   yet, so the static repoint could silently route Dopemux workflow calls\n   into another project while looking healthy. A warning comment now\n   guards the entry; design M10 is BLOCKED until P-24 or a fail-closed\n   identity-verifying wrapper exists.\n\nFocused suites: 72 passed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
