@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Summary\n\nPushes the next two **v5-exclusive** RTE-TRUTH security residual packets onto the series branch `claude/rte-audit-improvement-f4beb7` (same vehicle as closed #1043).\n\n### TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009 — F-30 residuals\n- Neutralize literal `</repo_content>` in untrusted bodies before wrap (tag-break escape)\n- Route `rte_ops_surfaces` cost-preview through `build_extraction_prompt_prefix`\n- Frame `llm_runtime` comparison lane with `UNTRUSTED_CONTENT_PREAMBLE`\n- Package-wide (non-legacy) single-literal preamble guard + **wiring pins** (R3-008 vacuous-test lesson)\n\n### TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010 — F-23 residuals\n- Expand sensitive-key fragments: `credential`, `passwd`, `access_key` (reject bare `cred`/`auth`)\n- **Document** short free-text secret residual honestly — do not claim structural impossibility\n- Security scrub on **raw/** partition payloads and **partX** shards (R3-007 only covered norm/)\n- Unify redaction token to `[REDACTED]` across prompts and scrub\n\n### Commits (tip)\n- `d0e9fd7ae7` fix(rte): TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009 — delimiter escape + preamble unification\n- `0181fc9e8b` fix(rte): TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010 — close F-23 residuals (raw, short secrets, token)\n\nAlso includes prior series work (R3-001…R3-008, R1, packets, etc.) on this branch.\n\n## Proof\n- `proof/rte-truth-program/TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-009/PROOF.json`\n- `proof/rte-truth-program/TP-RTE-TRUTH-R3-010/PROOF.json`\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `pytest services/repo-truth-extractor/tests/test_untrusted_content_delimiter.py`\n- [x] `pytest … -k 'delimiter or untrusted or preamble or comparison'`\n- [x] `pytest services/repo-truth-extractor/tests/test_write_time_secret_scrub.py`\n- [x] `pytest … test_secrets_redaction_binding.py test_output_safety.py`\n- [x] Mutation: identity neutralize reopens tag-break escape\n- [x] Mutation: disable raw partition scrub reopens bare-secret leak on raw/\n- [ ] CI on this PR\n\n## Notes / residuals\n- v5 exclusive (v3/v4 out of R3 scope; D-tier owns ports)\n- Short free-text secrets without key name or provider prefix remain **accepted residual**\n- ProcessPool worker `_op_write_json` still bypasses `write_json()` — pre-existing, not claimed closed","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-06-20T20:03:46Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-20T20:03:46Z","messageBody":"## Packet 4 — generic project-control exporter\n(`TP-DMX-PCP-CORE-GENERIC-EXPORTER-0001`)\n\nFirst **runtime-code** packet. A read-only `pcp export` that inspects\nany Git repository and emits a `project_evidence_export` JSON validating\nagainst the **de-Dopemux'd** core schema — with **no named-system\ndependency**.\n\n> **Stacked on #944 (Packet 3).** Base is the P3 branch until #944\nmerges to main, then I'll re-target this PR to `main` (clean — P4 is all\nnet-new files).\n\n### What it does\n- `src/dopemux/pcp/{exporter,cli}.py` — `export_evidence(repo_path)`\ndiscovers repo root, real `head_sha` (40/64-hex), branch\n(detached→null), dirty state; emits `generated_from_fixture=false` +\nreal `head_sha` (satisfies P3's runtime gate), all named-system sections\n`ABSENT`/`UNKNOWN` (fail-closed), `forbidden_action_confirmation` all\nfalse. **Self-validates** its output against the schema before\nreturning. `click` CLI (`python -m dopemux.pcp.cli export`).\n- **Read-only**: no writes, no network, no repo mutation.\n\n### Hardening (external PAL `gpt-5.2` review → PASS_WITH_RISKS, all 3\napplied)\n- Sanitized git env (strip `GIT_*`, `--no-pager`,\n`GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`, `GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, `-c\ncore.fsmonitor=false`) so a hostile repo config can't make git spawn an\nexternal helper.\n- NUL (`-z`) dirty-path parsing (correct for renames/quoted/spaced\npaths).\n- Accept SHA-1 **and** SHA-256 head_sha.\n\n### Validation\n**113 pytest pass** (12 new + 101 existing, no regressions); output\nself-validates; `export --help` works; pre-commit green.\n\nDraft / NEEDS_SUPERVISOR. Depends on Packet 3 (#944).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): Packet 4 — generic project-control exporter (#945)","oid":"924195d50381df5acfc67da090b9f348fee7771d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-20T20:04:13Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-20T20:04:13Z","messageBody":"## Packet 4.5 — executed negative-trap validation\n(`TP-DMX-PCP-FIXTURE-TO-RUNTIME-VALIDATION-0001`)\n\nExecutes (not asserts) fail-closed negative traps against the generic\nexporter and records a **failure index**. \"Executed, not asserted\" is\nenforced by schema (`executed: const true`).\n\n> **Stacked on #945 (Packet 4) → #944 (Packet 3).** Base re-targets up\nthe stack as each merges to main.\n\n### Contents\n- `schemas/project_control_plane/negative_case_result.schema.json` —\nfailure-index contract (executed `const true`; `result` enum; non-empty\nevidence fields; `additionalProperties:false`).\n- `src/dopemux/pcp/negative_cases.py` — `run_negative_traps()` executes\n5 traps (non-git dir, no-commit repo, runtime-missing-head_sha,\nold-Dopemux-field, secret-content-no-leak), captures real outcomes,\nself-validates output. `python -m dopemux.pcp.negative_cases`.\n- `reports/project-control-plane/validation/NEGATIVE_TRAPS_RESULT.json`\n— committed real run (5/5 PASS).\n- `tests/project_control_plane/test_negative_traps.py` (10 tests).\n\n### Validation\n**123 pytest pass**; runner 5/5 + self-validates; pre-commit green.\nExternal PAL `gpt-5.2` → PASS_WITH_RISKS; tightened evidence fields\n(`minLength`) applied. Follow-ups noted\n(symlink/submodule/LFS/determinism traps — the read-only exporter\nalready avoids content leak by design).\n\nDraft / NEEDS_SUPERVISOR. Depends on #945 (P4) + #944 (P3).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): Packet 4.5 — executed negative-trap validation (#946)","oid":"f4d56d55101b930eb94ed586a8d450b331ec4c94"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-22T00:20:41Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-22T00:20:41Z","messageBody":"…s (#951)\n\n## Summary\n\n`dopemux doctor` and `dopemux status` have crashed since **2026-04-05**\n(`efa82eca0`). The top-level `main()` handler swallows the exception\ninto ` Error: …` and exits 0, so the failures looked like silent no-ops.\nReal tracebacks (captured via `standalone_mode=False`):\n\n| Command | Error | Root cause |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dopemux doctor` | `ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected\n2, got 1)` | `_rich_doctor` (`cli.py`) passed a 1-tuple column\n`(\"Status\",)`; `styled_table` (`ui/theme.py`) only unpacked 2-tuples |\n| `dopemux status` | `KeyError: 'completed'` | status task loop read\n`task[\"completed\"]`/`[\"in_progress\"]`/`[\"name\"]`, but\n`TaskDecomposer.get_progress()` tasks expose `status` (string) +\n`description` |\n\nBoth are pre-existing on `main` (confirmed via `git blame`/`git show`),\nnot regressions from any feature branch.\n\n## Changes\n- `src/dopemux/ui/theme.py` — `styled_table` now accepts a bare\n`(name,)` column (defense-in-depth at a 47-caller shared helper; widened\ntype hint + docstring).\n- `src/dopemux/cli.py` — `status` task loop uses the real\n`status`/`description`/`progress` keys with `.get()` fallbacks.\n- `tests/test_cli_status_doctor_regression.py` — new; both tests fail on\nprior code, pass now.\n\n## Validation\n- **PASS** — 2 new regression tests; 34 existing+new CLI tests\n(`test_cli.py`), zero regressions; real `dopemux doctor` and `dopemux\nstatus` render cleanly.\n- **NOT_RUN** — full repo suite (scoped to CLI/theme for speed; changes\nare localized).\n\n## Not in this PR (operational / machine-local)\nSeparately, the global editable install was stale (pointed at a deleted\nworktree) and the `~/.local/bin/dopemux` wrapper failed outside a\ncheckout. Those were fixed locally (reinstall editable + wrapper\nfallback to the canonical checkout). A real follow-up is that\n`dopemux.cli` imports top-level `services.*`, which isn't part of the\ninstalled package — so the pip console script isn't standalone outside\nthe repo.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(cli): repair `dopemux doctor` and `dopemux status` runtime crashe…","oid":"91e82e23bf9f3b3eb6e567f00d5488c1e22685d3"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-22T00:21:01Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-22T00:21:01Z","messageBody":"## Packet 5 — DCP / Dopemux extension mapping (read/projection stage)\n\nAuthors the DCP extension as **instances** of the PCP Core contracts\nmerged in P2/P3. DCP = PCP Core + the Dopemux extension; this packet\nmaps existing Dopemux systems as **read/projection adapters** — nothing\nis promoted to authority, no live writes.\n\n### Deliverables\n- `schemas/dcp_extension/extension_manifest.dcp.json` — `DOPEMUX_DCP`\nmanifest; 5 invariants pinned `true`; owns only the two DCP schemas;\nforbids overriding the 3 core schemas.\n- `schemas/dcp_extension/authority_map.dcp.json` — **10** systems\n(task-orchestrator, conport, dope-memory, dope-context, dopecon-bridge,\nadhd-engine, repo-truth-extractor, dopetask, dopemux-cli, pr-steward) as\nderived surfaces: `live_write_allowed=false`, `canonical_writer=null`,\n`surface_class` ∈ {PROJECTION,ADAPTER,INDEX} (never SOURCE),\n`unknown_behavior=BLOCK_OR_ESCALATE`.\n- `tests/dcp_extension/test_dcp_extension_mapping.py` — 55 tests.\n- `docs/03-reference/dcp/dcp-extension-mapping.md`.\n\n### Scope decisions (grounded in the packet target + AIR §7)\n- **github-ci** — *not* mapped here; AIR §7 assigns GitHub/CI readiness\nto the **PR Steward proof-readiness** packet. (Removed during review;\nwas over-included in the first draft.)\n- **Leantime** — *not* mapped; named in AIR §4/§261 but has **no §7\ncomponent row** → mapping it would mean fabricating its contract role.\nDocumented as a deferred AIR follow-up.\n- **routing / OpenClaw / OpenRouter** — Packet 6.\n\n### Validation\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `pytest tests/dcp_extension/ tests/project_control_plane/` | **PASS**\n— 178 passed (55 dcp + 123 pcp, no regression) |\n| `jsonschema -i extension_manifest.dcp.json\n…/extension_manifest.schema.json` | **PASS** — valid |\n| `jsonschema -i authority_map.dcp.json …/authority_map.schema.json` |\n**PASS** — valid |\n| boundary check (all 10 entries read-only/derived, no SOURCE) |\n**PASS** — 0 violations |\n| `pre-commit run --files <changed>` (SKIP=docs-graph-validator) |\n**PASS** |\n\n### Review (codereview layer)\n- **PAL MCP was unavailable this session** (server not connected) and\nnative `advisor()` is not loaded → codereview was done by (a) my own\nOpus entry-by-entry semantic review and (b) an **independent Sonnet\nadversarial reviewer** (isolated context, read the actual files +\non-main contracts + AIR §7). Verdict: **APPROVE_WITH_NITS**.\n- Reviewer findings actioned: doc overclaim corrected (the generic\nschema permits `SOURCE`+live-write — DCP's read-only property is\nenforced by the **DCP test guard**, now proven by\n`test_source_write_escalation_caught_by_dcp_guard`); `dopecon-bridge`\nsource ref deepened to the upstream event store;\n`compatible_pcp_core_versions` corrected to the 3 core contract\nversions; github-ci scope-removed; Leantime documented as deferred.\n\n### Residual risk / UNKNOWNs\n- AIR internal inconsistency (Leantime in §4/§261, absent from §7) is\n**documented, not resolved** — needs an operator/architecture decision\non whether Leantime gets a §7 row.\n- The all-read-only DCP property is enforced by the packet's test suite,\n**not** by the generic core schema (by PCP Core design). A future\nDCP-specific schema could harden this structurally if desired (out of P5\nscope).\n\nPacket: `task-packets/generated/TP-DMX-DCP-EXTENSION-MAPPING-0001.json`\n· Worktree `.claude/worktrees/pcp-p5` · Branch\n`claude/pcp-p5-dcp-extension-mapping`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): DCP extension mapping instances (Packet 5) (#950)","oid":"7505d47fa097f9dc8a8cd67977f28e2c0ecb2fea"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-22T19:08:31Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-22T19:08:31Z","messageBody":"## Summary\n- adds TP-DMX-COCKPIT-ELECTRIC-REFRESH-RUNTIME-001 and proof notes\n- adds deterministic five-mode cockpit rendering via render_cockpit()\nand SUPPORTED_COCKPIT_MODES\n- expands cockpit run --mode to pm, implementer, overview, services,\nevents while preserving guarded runtime-render behavior\n\n## Validation\n- python -m jsonschema -i\ntask-packets/generated/TP-DMX-COCKPIT-ELECTRIC-REFRESH-RUNTIME-001.json\ndocs/03-reference/spec/dopetask/dopetask-canonical-spec.json\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest tests/unit/dopemux/ui/cockpit\ntests/unit/test_cockpit_cli.py tests/test_cockpit_tokens.py -q\n- PYTHONPATH=src python -m compileall -q src/dopemux tests\n- git 