group across 1 directory with 3 updates (#943)","oid":"2796e96e6ebe22cdb5bb4534017d05a0e7be7dde"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T03:43:29Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:01:54Z","messageBody":"…outes\n\nPR Steward MUST_FIX Item 1 from #931 was the one of seven not carried into\nthe canonical #953/#954 OpenClaw DCP routing contracts. The top-level\nopenrouter_profile allowed null, and the only enforcement of a named profile\nwas keyed on provider == \"openrouter\". A SELECTED decision with\naccess_path == \"openrouter_paid\" but provider set to any other value (e.g.\n\"openai\", \"unknown\") could therefore carry openrouter_profile: null and\nbypass every per-profile allowlist — even though openclaw_dcp_routing_policy.yaml\nrequires openrouter_profile evidence for OpenRouter routes.\n\nAdd an allOf conditional to route_decision.schema.json requiring a named\n(non-null) openrouter_profile whenever decision_status == \"SELECTED\" AND\naccess_path == \"openrouter_paid\", bound to the six named profiles. The guard\nkeys on access_path (the routing plane), so it holds regardless of provider.\n\nAdd a negative regression test: SELECTED + openrouter_paid + null profile must\nfail for provider in {openrouter, openai, unknown}; the named-profile baseline\nand all R0-R6 + UNKNOWN example decisions still validate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(contracts): enforce named openrouter_profile on openrouter_paid r…","oid":"fa4c792682ed074017cd00a80ca37799f1f145d7"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:11:19Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:11:19Z","messageBody":"…tatus_map\n\nA2 proof-family follow-up (exporter-consumption). New dopemux.pcp.dcp_extension_export\nmodule WRAPS the generic, project-agnostic dopemux.pcp.exporter.export_evidence (does\nNOT modify it) and, when the target repo carries the DCP extension manifest, resolves\nthe declared proof_status_mappings -> proof_status_map -> proof_pointers and enriches\nthe export's proof_manifest from real repo state (PRESENT/ABSENT + path), keeping the\nresult schema-valid. No import-time file I/O (wheel-safe). Generic export returned\nunchanged when no DCP extension is present.\n\nIncrement 1 = presence resolution; SHA-based freshness (CURRENT/STALE) deferred\n(proof-bundle formats are heterogeneous, no canonical schema yet) -> freshness=UNKNOWN.\n\nTests: tests/project_control_plane/test_dcp_extension_export.py (3) — generic fallback,\nDCP-present-proof, DCP-absent-proof; all assert enriched output validates against\nproject_evidence_export.schema.json.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(dcp): DCP-aware export seam — enrich proof_manifest from proof_s…","oid":"2d2a481a4439972cbb45a60e270668642a58b942"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:04:58Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:16:21Z","messageBody":"- Add missing closing </Tooltip> tag\n- Wrap multiple children in a single Box to satisfy MUI requirement\n- Improve hover interaction area for team load insight\n\nCo-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\t.Jules/palette.md\n#\tui-dashboard/src/components/TeamDashboard.tsx","messageHeadline":"palette: fix invalid Tooltip and JSX in TeamDashboard","oid":"88521748317aae8a9f4d43d64acdcc164ba322b5"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T05:59:01Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"hu3mann"},{"email":"161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","id":"BOT_kgDOCZ5PDw","login":"google-labs-jules[bot]","name":"google-labs-jules[bot]"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:16:21Z","messageBody":"- Wraps multiple children in a single Box to satisfy MUI Tooltip requirements.\n- Fixes unclosed Tooltip tag that caused JSX errors.\n- Improves accessibility by providing a consolidated interactive surface.\n- Updates Palette journal with MUI child constraint findings.\n\nCo-authored-by: google-labs-jules[bot] <161369871+google-labs-jules[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(ui): correct TeamDashboard Tooltip structure and JSX syntax","oid":"67c2eab24f306e484cd042dda3ed84e408540789"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:10:58Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com","id":"BOT_kgDODVMyew","login":"Copilot","name":"Copilot"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:16:21Z","messageBody":"… repo catalog semantics)\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","messageHeadline":"mcp: align bundled default task-orchestrator to HTTP transport (match…","oid":"ade600146522407cb1ab866ba05b7874a2f47cf2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:24:38Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:24:38Z","messageBody":"Completes the A2 follow-up the #977 DROP_FROM_PR1 ruling deferred: 'model proof.*\nownership cleanly (not the MCP adapter set)'. Adds the proof.dopemux_family authority\nentry (owner = the project itself; read-only ADAPTER over PROOF.json/SUMMARY.md;\ncanonical_writer null; live_write_allowed false; BLOCK_OR_ESCALATE).\n\nThe Packet-5 scope-lock is refined to a TWO-PLANE guard keyed by domain prefix:\n  - ADAPTER plane (the 11 MCP-system owners) — EXPECTED_SYSTEMS and adapter_mappings\n    UNCHANGED (no 'dopemux' added) → the operator's protected scope-lock is preserved.\n  - PROOF-FAMILY plane (proof.* domains) — guarded separately; NOT in adapter_mappings.\n\nThis is the clean model the deferral called for: proof artifacts are owned by the\nproject, not an external MCP adapter, so they get their own plane rather than being\nforced into (and bumping) the adapter set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(dcp): model proof-family authority as a distinct plane","oid":"bff8657d03f6f44b30053f9b38ad124286c9da7f"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:44:46Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:44:46Z","messageBody":"…p binding\n\nPorts #975's net-new A1 activation layer onto the surgical stack, reconciled onto\n#978 wheel-safe schema loading (drops #975's competing _load_validator dual-path).\n\nTwo fail-closed gates run in route_mutation ONLY when execute is True AND a writer\nis registered (inert behaviour unchanged — no writer ⇒ gates never fire):\n  - 6b assertion verification: default NoTrustedIssuerVerifier rejects\n    (ASSERTION_ISSUER_UNTRUSTED); a real signed-issuer verifier is injected at\n    activation. Verifier exceptions fail closed.\n  - 6c authority-map binding: default FailClosedAuthorityBinding rejects\n    (AUTHORITY_MAP_ABSENT); binding_from_entries requires a SOURCE entry with\n    live_write_allowed=true + BLOCK_OR_ESCALATE. The DCP map has no SOURCE entries\n    by design, so live writes stay impossible there.\n\nroute_mutation / create_bridge_router / create_bridge_app gain assertion_verifier +\nauthority_binding params (default None ⇒ fail-closed defaults). New modules:\nassertion_auth.py, authority_binding.py.\n\nTests (grok's reconcile, validated against this port): LIVE-path tests inject a\npass-verifier + binding_from_entries; new gate tests; inert-CLI tests. Full\ntests/project_control_plane green incl. #978 parity + Red Line #15 guard.\n\nDeferred (additive, not load-bearing for the fail-closed default): optional\nissuer/signature fields on live_write_ready.schema.json for real signed assertions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): A1 activation gates — signed-READY verifier + authority-ma…","oid":"77af56781e79330143d3735bdb4c9bd25e3eb721"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:47:07Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T06:47:07Z","messageBody":"…ED (#968/#967)\n\nCloses the #968/#967 routing residual the supervisor tracked: the SELECTED branch\npreviously permitted selected_provider=='unknown'. Minimal STRICT change — drop\n'unknown' from the SELECTED-branch enum only; the base enum is unchanged. A chosen\nroute must name a real provider.\n\nDeliberately NOT #975's wholesale route_decision rewrite (which added ~13 new\nrequired fields and would break every existing route_decision instance). No fixture\npins selected_provider=='unknown', so this breaks nothing.\n\nTests: TestSelectedProviderResidual (reject unknown under SELECTED; baseline still valid).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(dcp): STRICT routing residual — forbid unknown provider on SELECT…","oid":"f42b69cfb6ee29b4d4d89e62f72f2bbe1cc7508d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T07:01:40Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:01:40Z","messageBody":"…eadiness)\n\nAdditive (not required): issuer, issued_at, key_id, signature_alg, signature,\nauthenticity — slots for a real signed READY issuer to populate. Schema-presence\nonly: authenticity is decided by the injected bridge verifier (assertion_auth),\nNEVER by the schema. Default NoTrustedIssuerVerifier still rejects regardless.\n\nApplied to BOTH the canonical schema and the #978 vendored copy (byte-identical;\nparity test enforces). Completes the deferred A1 follow-on from #986.\n\nTest: a READY assertion carrying the signed fields validates (additive, non-breaking).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): optional signed-assertion fields on live_write_ready (A1 r…","oid":"bf6fbed00bd03004a44d8fd3eaf194a777219d85"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T07:05:34Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:05:34Z","messageBody":"Resolves the deferred freshness increment for the #985 export seam. When a declared\nproof root is present, the seam reads it and compares a recorded head-SHA field\n(dopemux PROOF.json uses 'head'; also accepts head_sha/git_sha/commit_sha/commit/sha)\nto the export's repo_state.head_sha → proof_manifest.freshness = CURRENT (match) /\nSTALE (differ) / UNKNOWN (not JSON or no recognized SHA field — never guessed).\n\nHonest over heterogeneous proof formats: only a recognized field yields CURRENT/STALE.\n\nTests: head==current → CURRENT; head!=current → STALE (added); the no-SHA proof case\nstill yields UNKNOWN (unchanged).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(dcp): SHA-based proof freshness in the DCP export seam","oid":"0ad49fd257a284b42236b50b750e83d50acaee6d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T21:25:18Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(pcp): package dopemux.pcp + dopemux-pcp console script","oid":"f85b92d26abee8f1158b3561b4d687e66b088d49"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T21:29:02Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"… entry)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(dcp): deliver proof-family mapping (proof_status_map + authority…","oid":"4468bbc5c830f5315728ae5710444ac41284b65a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T21:29:56Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"test(pcp): regression guard for AIR Red Line #15","oid":"fa85095c93ba024549b9fe5c8cae56dc9b0d154d"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T21:31:53Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Sonnet 4.6"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(pcp): fix bridge runbook param + conformance classification note","oid":"869f0ba81b26fc83a509bcc801cad338027c0a69"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T21:59:16Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"…ope-lock)\n\nOperator ruling DROP_FROM_PR1: the optional proof.dopemux_family authority-map\nentry collided with the Packet-5 scope-lock (owners ≡ adapter_mappings ≡\nEXPECTED_SYSTEMS, all MCP-system adapters). Registering 'dopemux' as a pseudo-\nadapter to satisfy the lock blurs adapter-ownership vs proof-family-ownership.\n\nKeep the core A2 deliverable (proof_status_map.dcp.json artifact + manifest\nproof_status_mappings + non-empty/pointer-valid tests). Defer proof-family\nauthority modeling to the A2 exporter-consumption follow-up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(dcp): drop proof.* authority entry from PR1 (preserve Packet-5 sc…","oid":"4e46892d23270273a9aca37b82a3d4f7c6c08fcc"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-23T22:15:26Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"…2 scope-lock-preserved\n\n- A4: packaging declared (wheel ships pcp + console script, PROVEN) but installed\n  import still blocked by repo-root schema loading in 4 modules → tracked follow-up\n  'PCP wheel-safe schema loading'. Clean-venv import gate = FAIL (known/deferred).\n- A2: reflect DROP_FROM_PR1 (no proof.* authority entry; Packet-5 scope-lock intact);\n  2 proof_status_map tests; authority modeling deferred.\n- Honest validation buckets (wheel CONTENTS pass, clean-venv import fail).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(pcp): correct audit note — A4 PARTIAL (wheel-import deferred), A…","oid":"b875e9e0d810e4ba56ccded3a9f952a0817a3c84"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T05:48:02Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"…#978)\n\n## What & why\nThe four `dopemux.pcp` modules (`exporter`, `negative_cases`,\n`pr_steward`, `bridge.fastapi_bridge`) loaded their JSON Schema **at\nimport time** via a repo-root-relative path (`parents[N]` from\n`__file__`). That path does not exist in an installed wheel, so\nimporting `dopemux.pcp.*` from a `pip install`-ed dopemux crashed with\n`FileNotFoundError`.\n\nThis completes **Tracked Follow-up #1** (A4 wheel-import) deferred by\nthe conformance repair on this base branch.\n\n## Changes\n**1. Bundle PCP schemas as package data**\n- Vendor the 4 loaded schemas under `dopemux/pcp/_schemas/` + a\n`load_schema()` shim using `importlib.resources` (resolves identically\nfrom the source tree and an installed wheel — single path, no repo-root\nassumption).\n- Repoint the 4 loaders at `load_schema(...)`; drop the now-dead\n`json`/`pathlib` imports.\n- `pyproject.toml`: add `dopemux.pcp._schemas` to `packages` +\n`package-data = [\"*.json\"]`.\n- New parity test: vendored copies must stay **byte-identical** to\ncanonical `schemas/project_control_plane/` (the modules validate against\ntheir copy, so drift would ship a stale contract).\n\n**2. Declare `jsonschema` as a core dependency**\n- The 4 shipped pcp modules `import jsonschema` directly, but it was\nonly in the `test`/`dev` extras — a clean install got it only\ntransitively via `litellm`. Declared `jsonschema>=4.20.0` in core\n`dependencies` so the import chain cannot break if litellm ever changes.\nVerified `Requires-Dist: jsonschema>=4.20.0` now appears unconditionally\nin the wheel METADATA.\n\nNo PCP/DCP runtime logic changed.\n\n## Verification\n- `tests/project_control_plane` + `tests/dcp_extension`: **435 passed, 0\nfailed**.\n- Parity test: RED (`FileNotFoundError`) → GREEN after vendoring.\n- Clean-venv wheel install (`--no-deps` + import-time deps): all 6\n`dopemux.pcp.*` imports OK from `site-packages`; schemas resolve from\n`site-packages/dopemux/pcp/_schemas`; `dopemux-pcp export --help` runs.\n- Wheel contents include `dopemux/pcp/*`, all 4 `_schemas/*.json`, and\nthe `dopemux-pcp` entry point; METADATA declares `Requires-Dist:\njsonschema>=4.20.0`.\n\n## Base\nRebased onto `claude/pcp-conformance-repair-0001` (which adds the\n`dopemux.pcp` allowlist + `dopemux-pcp` console script). Targets that\nbranch, not `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(pcp): bundle PCP schemas as package data for wheel-safe imports (…","oid":"279da2ecb401c44ac77f2b579782819b9c86a839"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-24T05:54:38Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"The clean-venv import gate (FAIL in the partial state) now PASSES on the merged\nbranch: wheel bundles the 4 vendored schemas + loader shim, jsonschema is a core\ndep, and all 6 dopemux.pcp.* modules import from an installed wheel. Updates the\nA4 classification PARTIAL→FIXED, the validation buckets, and the follow-up list\n(wheel-safety completed by #978; A2 authority/exporter + routing + A1 remain).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(pcp): A4 FIXED — wheel-safe schema loading folded in via #978","oid":"a9a076ff8bdac37e6b871db05780d07677495b78"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T06:55:56Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T07:25:20Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"chore: update audit report frontmatter and lockfile post-rebase","oid":"8080e068c4ea0c066a52670f8deaaba26d3298