":"e445c348f0b2aaad6dff810144e318c6852fc5d3"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:30Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:30Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/feat/rte-cost-profile-alignment'","oid":"ec0d37205622bd7467f6ad9aa11308d0cc970863"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:36Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:36Z","messageBody":"…8958489781780458'\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\t.Jules/palette.md","messageHeadline":"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/palette/prediction-panel-ux-1563…","oid":"318761f092a1b806bf0628cfcce5665322078e42"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:55Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T10:35:55Z","messageBody":"…3344074350353909579'\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\t.Jules/palette.md\n#\tui-dashboard/src/components/TeamDashboard.tsx\n#\tui-dashboard/src/components/__tests__/Accessibility.test.tsx","messageHeadline":"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/palette-team-dashboard-refactor-…","oid":"a90b8777adc58ae937d00fdeae191f517df4d2d0"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T10:36:13Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T10:36:13Z","messageBody":"# Conflicts:\n#\tdocs/05-audit-reports/pcp-dcp-conformance-2026-06-23.md\n#\ttests/dcp_extension/test_proof_status_map.py\n#\ttests/project_control_plane/test_packaging.py\n#\ttests/project_control_plane/test_red_line_15.py","messageHeadline":"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/claude/pcp-a2-proof-family'","oid":"b010fdd125bf2b3cbc6e3047f04d3185036a58b6"},{"authoredDate":"2026-06-27T10:36:14Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"}],"committedDate":"2026-06-27T10:36:14Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/claude/pcp-a1-activation-routing'","oid":"c367cdbbf8ffc9c222e5dcf6e3b4b0ded3ff987e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:03Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:03Z","messageBody":"Eight-agent read-only audit of the full MCP server fleet: canonical\nfeature register, per-server design-vs-implementation gap matrices,\noptimal interaction model, and a phased target-state plan.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(mcp): add MCP fleet canonical audit + target-state design","oid":"ea7c9455c9299d166c6ca19ae900f34fded51f79"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","messageBody":"…eFailure\n\nnative_hooks previously emitted only content-free heartbeat pings to the\ndopemux:events stream, which the dope-memory promotion engine does not\nconsume, leaving the chronicle's work_log_entries empty. Wire the\nPostToolUseFailure handler to the deterministic capture spine\n(capture_client.emit_capture_event) with event_type=error.encountered,\nthe one hook-available type on the WMA promotion allowlist. Fail-open:\ncapture errors never propagate to the session. Session/file-edit events\nare intentionally NOT wired — they are heartbeat (non-promotable) and\nwould recreate the spam this fixes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(hooks): emit promotable error.encountered capture from PostToolUs…","oid":"a8cd7e9b3c1173347791f8e23571022e29f89ac4"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","messageBody":"_ensure_schema() logged a warning and proceeded when post-apply\nverification could not confirm the workspace_contexts table, and the\nsuccess log sat inside the failure branch. Raise RuntimeError to abort\nstartup when verification fails, and move the success log to the success\npath. Idempotent 'already exists' applies are unaffected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(conport): fail closed on unverifiable schema post-apply check","oid":"dbe6b13ec35cc0dd284af0ca4c4a9804af14bad4"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","messageBody":"pal used 'test: exit 0' (always green) and dope-context used\n'curl ... || exit 0' (masks a dead server). Use the real /health probe\nfor pal (matching its Dockerfile) and change dope-context to '|| exit 1'.\nUncomment the dope-context /health custom_route so the probe has an\nendpoint to hit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(mcp): replace fake healthchecks for pal and dope-context","oid":"75c8ee60d49f6ea276f7bda00b4f1b99aebe96c2"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","messageBody":"…servers\n\nFour keys appeared twice; YAML last-wins flipped desktop-commander,\ngpt-researcher, and leantime-bridge to default_enabled: false despite\ncompose deploying them active (pal was an exact dup). Keep the single\nenabled occurrence matching compose deployment state.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(mcp): remove duplicate registry.yaml keys that silently disabled …","oid":"dbb7f6ccaa67b01be41ff4dbcd00d86bdb95a06f"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:04Z","messageBody":"…iner\n\nThe load-bearing PAL container (Codex declares it required=true) has no\nensure/restart script and vanishes on docker prune. Add an idempotent\nensure script: fast-exit if running, start if stopped, run if absent,\nfail closed (non-zero, no silent success) if the daemon is down or the\nimage is missing. Supports --recreate for recovery.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"feat(mcp): add ensure-pal.sh for the off-compose pal-mcp-server conta…","oid":"bd9a6f380692c26f1e42e56537df2a2670275cab"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:32Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:05:32Z","messageBody":"The 'one import populates the chronicle' claim was over-optimistic:\nsession/file-edit events are not on the WMA promotion allowlist, so\nhooks can only contribute error.encountered. Chronicle population\nrequires wiring decision.logged / task.* / workflow.phase_changed at\ntheir sources.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(mcp): correct chronicle-fix claim per promotion allowlist reality","oid":"79340f854743e9fac219bbcdd607ee91bcd7bdbe"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:22:56Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:22:56Z","messageBody":"…c pal build hint\n\ndope-context /health now returns {status:healthy, service, version,\ntimestamp} matching the registry health contract used by other services\n(was {status: ok}). ensure-pal.sh's missing-image hint no longer\nhard-codes a developer-specific checkout path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(mcp): address Copilot review — fleet-shape health payload, generi…","oid":"69c79fcb1013624fb58981b55f02d5fd53e1a82b"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-03T13:25:37Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-03T13:25:37Z","messageBody":"The PAL HTTP wrapper's /health always sent HTTP 200, so 'curl -f' (the\ncontainer healthcheck) reported healthy even after the wrapped server.py\nsubprocess exited. Compute health first and return 503 on the unhealthy\nbranch so Docker and health collectors actually observe the failure.\nAddresses Codex review on the mcp-pal healthcheck.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"fix(pal): return 503 from /health when MCP subprocess is dead","oid":"b226fdb4d224ee2ecb0c7bcde3e1d9624c15696e"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-04T03:34:24Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T03:34:24Z","messageBody":"Merge PR #995.\\n\\nSummary:\\n- Add packetized MCP fleet roadmap Lane 1.\\n- Add canonical MCP catalog schema and static drift gates.\\n- Fix catalog, legacy registry, command-surface, and bundled fallback catalog drift.\\n\\nValidation:\\n- GitHub CI green.\\n- Review conversations resolved.\\n- Focused local catalog and MCP/compose tests passed before merge.","messageHeadline":"test(mcp): gate canonical fleet catalog drift","oid":"98c43ef3b01b28aafb6fadc4d6a4dc7d1cf2dde0"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-04T04:02:47Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"Dj Dom"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T04:02:47Z","messageBody":"## Summary\n- add deterministic MCP fleet output renderers backed by\n`mcp_catalog.yaml`\n- add `dopemux mcp generate` with dry-run as the default and `--apply\n--output-dir` required for writes\n- document generated output surfaces and record Lane 2 proof notes\n\n## Authority / Scope\n- Implements `TP-DMX-MCP-FLEET-ROADMAP-002-GENERATED-OUTPUTS`\n- Depends on merged Lane 1 catalog contract and drift gates\n- Static generation only: no Docker mutation, live MCP probes, provider\ncalls, or user-global writes\n\n## Validation\nPASS:\n- `python -m jsonschema -i\ntask-packets/generated/TP-DMX-MCP-FLEET-ROADMAP-002-GENERATED-OUTPUTS.json\ndocs/03-reference/spec/dopetask/dopetask-canonical-spec.json`\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_commands_catalog.py\ntests/unit/test_mcp_fleet_catalog.py -q`\n- `python -m pytest tests/arch/test_mcp_fleet_catalog_contract.py -q`\n- `python -m py_compile src/dopemux/mcp/fleet_catalog.py\nsrc/dopemux/commands/mcp_commands.py`\n- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m dopemux.cli mcp --help`\n- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m dopemux.cli mcp generate --output-dir\n/tmp/dmx-mcp-generated-smoke`\n- `PYTHONPATH=src python -m dopemux.cli mcp generate --apply\n--output-dir /tmp/dmx-mcp-generated-smoke-lane2`\n- `find /tmp/dmx-mcp-generated-smoke-lane2 -type f | sort`\n- `python -c 'import pathlib, tomllib;\ntomllib.loads(pathlib.Path(\"/tmp/dmx-mcp-generated-smoke-lane2/codex/config.toml\").read_text())'`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `pre-commit run --files src/dopemux/commands/mcp_commands.py\nsrc/dopemux/mcp/fleet_catalog.py tests/unit/test_mcp_commands_catalog.py\ntests/unit/test_mcp_fleet_catalog.py\ndocs/03-reference/mcp/fleet-generated-outputs.md\ntask-packets/generated/TP-DMX-MCP-FLEET-ROADMAP-002-GENERATED-OUTPUTS.json\nproof/dmx-mcp-fleet-roadmap/TP-DMX-MCP-FLEET-ROADMAP-002-GENERATED-OUTPUTS/implementation-notes.md`\n\nNOT_RUN:\n- Docker health and live MCP ini