c/pydantic/releases/tag/v2.13.0\">GitHub release</a></p>\n<p>The highlights of the v2.13 release are available in the <a href=\"https://pydantic.dev/articles/pydantic-v2-13-release\">blog post</a>.</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/cf67d4b3193c3fe43ede18612ed62785eee11382\"><code>cf67d4b</code></a> Fix linting</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/f0d8a214a5803036db46a56b1f62f1e56b81d662\"><code>f0d8a21</code></a> Prepare release v2.13.4</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/5e3fe1d41a00f441204241c66078003ae0391f9a\"><code>5e3fe1d</code></a> Check for pydantic tag pattern in CI</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/7f9edcc2a191d2eaa9751220eb910914e716a686\"><code>7f9edcc</code></a> Document tagging conventions</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/b46a0c9b8a4dd967fda8ec1a92f6437076bf262c\"><code>b46a0c9</code></a> Adapt <code>pydantic-core</code> linker flags on macOS</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/50629c851e61d887d5420452c311ec6203f1f400\"><code>50629c8</code></a> Update to PyPy 7.3.22</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/8522ebb71e5e9a6f7188af5f009f01785b8cf725\"><code>8522ebb</code></a> Preserve <code>RootModel</code> core metadata</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/a37f3aff090ca342dc5f48304889963530b993f8\"><code>a37f3af</code></a> Adapt <code>MISSING</code> sentinel test to work with unreleased <code>typing_extensions</code> ver...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/909259a9df660518033aa686b689f045a6eaf9d2\"><code>909259a</code></a> Remove Logfire example in documentation</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/commit/2c4174c366606fc2dc46cb806833a080aefa77df\"><code>2c4174c</code></a> Bump libc from 0.2.155 to 0.2.185</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/compare/v2.12.5...v2.13.4\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `docker` from 7.1.0 to 7.2.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/docker/docker-py/releases\">docker's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>7.2.0</h2>\n<h2>Upgrade Notes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>docker.from_env()</code> now honors the active Docker CLI context when <code>DOCKER_HOST</code> is not set.\n<ul>\n<li>This means the client may connect to the daemon selected by <code>DOCKER_CONTEXT</code> or the current context in <code>~/.docker/config.json</code>, matching Docker CLI behavior more closely.</li>\n<li>If your application relied on the previous default connection behavior, set <code>DOCKER_HOST</code> explicitly, set <code>DOCKER_CONTEXT=default</code>, or pass <code>use_context=False</code> to <code>DockerClient.from_env()</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Added <code>docker.from_context()</code> / <code>DockerClient.from_context()</code> for explicitly creating a client from a Docker CLI context.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Added support for Docker contexts when creating the default client</li>\n<li>Added subpath support for volumes</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Bugfixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed <code>exec_run</code> documentation for the <code>stream</code> parameter</li>\n<li>Fixed image loading to avoid depending on the deprecated <code>JSONMessage.error</code> field</li>\n<li>Preserved the rotated unlock key in swarm integration tests</li>\n<li>Fixed SSL certificate generation in tests</li>\n<li>Fixed IPv6 integration tests by explicitly enabling IPv6 where required</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Miscellaneous</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Updated tests for newer Docker Engine behavior</li>\n<li>CI and build updates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>tests/exec: expect 127 exit code for missing executable by <a href=\"https://github.com/laurazard\"><code>@​laurazard</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3290\">docker/docker-py#3290</a></li>\n<li>fixing doc for stream param in exec_run by <a href=\"https://github.com/yasonk\"><code>@​yasonk</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3292\">docker/docker-py#3292</a></li>\n<li>Bump default API version to 1.45 (Moby 26.0/26.1) by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3261\">docker/docker-py#3261</a></li>\n<li>Set a dummy-version if none set, and remove unused APT_MIRROR build-arg by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3267\">docker/docker-py#3267</a></li>\n<li>test_service_logs: stop testing experimental versions by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/2442\">docker/docker-py#2442</a></li>\n<li>Makefile: fix circular reference for integration-dind by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3297\">docker/docker-py#3297</a></li>\n<li>image load: don't depend on deprecated JSONMessage.error field by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3307\">docker/docker-py#3307</a></li>\n<li>integration: test_create_volume_invalid_driver allow either 400 or 404 by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3296\">docker/docker-py#3296</a></li>\n<li>integration: adjust tests for omitted &quot;OnBuild&quot; by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3336\">docker/docker-py#3336</a></li>\n<li>Implement Subpath Support for Volumes in Docker-Py (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/issues/3243\">#3243</a>) by <a href=\"https://github.com/Khushiyant\"><code>@​Khushiyant</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3270\">docker/docker-py#3270</a></li>\n<li>tests: fix ssl generation by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3365\">docker/docker-py#3365</a></li>\n<li>test/integration: don't check for deprecated Networks field by <a href=\"https://github.com/thaJeztah\"><code>@​thaJeztah</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3362\">docker/docker-py#3362</a></li>\n<li>test: Skip from_env_unix tests if DOCKER_HOST is network socket by <a href=\"https://github.com/ricardobranco777\"><code>@​ricardobranco777</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3366\">docker/docker-py#3366</a></li>\n<li>test_connect_with_ipv6_address: enable IPv6 by <a href=\"https://github.com/robmry\"><code>@​robmry</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3372\">docker/docker-py#3372</a></li>\n<li>test_create_with_ipv6_address: enable IPv6 by <a href=\"https://github.com/robmry\"><code>@​robmry</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3373\">docker/docker-py#3373</a></li>\n<li>tests: Migrate off gpg2 and regenerate key ed25519 by <a href=\"https://github.com/vvoland\"><code>@​vvoland</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3399\">docker/docker-py#3399</a></li>\n<li>gha: Pin to digests by <a href=\"https://github.com/vvoland\"><code>@​vvoland</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/docker/docker-py/pull/3408\">docker/docker-py#3408</a></li>\n<li>Fix integration tests on non-amd64 hosts and add ARM64 C