+{"additions":1264,"baseRefName":"main","body":"## MCP fleet multi-instance design + P-22/P-23 safe-subset implementation\n\n**Scope disclosure (per supervisor disposition)**: this branch is **not design-only**. It contains:\n1. The governing design + evidence base (`claudedocs/mcp-fleet-multi-instance-{design,evidence}-2026-07-28.md`), **ACCEPTED with supervisor rulings D1–D4 applied** (design §10), plus the supervisor **repair pass** (commit edb265c963).\n2. **P-22 safe subset (implementation)**: 14 legacy fleet launch scripts / compose overlays deleted (2,521 deleted lines are intentional — see label); runtime callers repaired (`dopemux mcp up` no longer shells out to a deleted script; `provision.py` stack sentinel swapped); CI guard test `tests/mcp/test_no_legacy_fleet_start_paths.py` added.\n3. **P-23 safe subset (docs)**: AGENTS.md §12.6 sharing-class table, `.claude/claude.md` fleet rules, stale pre-#1052 catch-22 workaround removed, lettered A–E model deprecation-bannered, ~40 reader-facing docs corrected (`:8000` shadow twin vs `:7890` MCP surface, `registry.yaml` deprecation).\n4. **M10: attempted then REVERTED** (supervisor repair 3): the `.vibe/config.toml` repoint to `127.0.0.1:7890` was reverted because that port is currently held by the dNh_CRM task-orchestrator and no identity-aware switch mechanism exists yet — a static URL would silently route this repo's workflow calls into another project. A warning comment now guards the entry; M10 is blocked until P-24 or a fail-closed identity-verifying wrapper.\n\n### Supervisor rulings baked into the design (2026-07-28)\n- **D1**: Kotlin TO end-state = **project-scoped leased-port instances** (new ADR required, packet P-24); `multi_project_singleton` NOT authorized; `switch-project` transitional only. Corrected record: PR #1086 was closed for bundling an unapproved authority change — governance rejection, not technical proof.\n- **D2**: python `:8000` service will be **renamed** (candidate `dopemux-workflow-api`), not retired — DopeconBridge and workflow surfaces depend on it (rewritten M11).\n- **D3**: ConPort end-state = **project-scoped**, never host-singleton; CRS v2/P-18 rewritten around a fixed project tenant with the wall enforced in storage.\n- **D4**: redis-events REQUIRED target = **project-scoped**; P-21 elevated to P0. **OBSERVED runtime today remains an unsafe host singleton** — no P-21 implementation is in this branch; docs state observed-vs-required explicitly (supervisor repair 1).\n\n### Migration status\n`GO_M0_ONLY` — M0 snapshots executed to `~/.dopemux/backup/` (containers, volumes, lease registry, pal container inspects). M0 status per supervisor: CLAIMED_COMPLETE (snapshots are operator-local, not independently verified). **M3 is BLOCKED with rollback UNKNOWN** (supervisor repair 2): its previously stated rollback source (`/private/tmp/pal-model-refresh` compose) no longer exists; a bounded recreation-proof packet (pinned `ensure-pal.sh` revision, image digest, mounts/env, shadow-name recreation, health + Codex `docker exec` verification) is required first. M1–M5 remain blocked pending P-07/P-10 implementation.\n\n### Validation\n- PASS: `tests/mcp/` + CLI startup + health-probe suites (72 tests at head edb265c963); removal commit additionally validated against 168 tests incl. unit/arch suites; guard test passes.\n- NOT_RUN: full repo suite; any blocked migration step.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","changedFiles":56,"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-07-28T22:48:44Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-28T22:48:44Z","messageBody":"…worklist\n\nDesign for multi-project/multi-worktree MCP fleet operation: sharing\nclasses per server (interim vs end-state gated on MEMSPINE-IDENTITY-005\nand ConPort CRS v2), single identity module, port/lease GC, discovery\nsnapshot + TRANSIENT/OWNERSHIP finding split, adoption path, 16-step\nmigration, 23 Sonnet-implementable packets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"docs(mcp): multi-instance fleet design + evidence base + legacy-path …","oid":"c72ea5950a2a73c1b51110df0130532345070013"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-28T23:06:00Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-28T23:06:00Z","messageBody":"Removes the duplicate/dead MCP fleet start scripts and legacy compose\noverlays identified by claudedocs/mcp-legacy-launch-path-worklist-2026-07-28.md,\nper the P-22 packet in claudedocs/mcp-fleet-multi-instance-design-2026-07-28.md §9.\n\nDeleted (14 files covering all 15 worklist paths — docker/mcp-servers/ is a\ngit-tracked symlink to docker/mcp-servers-source/, so the two worklist\nentries for start-all-mcp-servers.sh under those paths are the same file):\n- scripts/start-all-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/manage-mcp-servers.sh, scripts/mcp/manage-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/install-docker-mcp-servers.sh\n- scripts/deploy/deployment/{start-all,start-mcp-servers,stack_up_all}.sh\n- scripts/memory/start-memory-stack.sh\n- scripts/setup.sh\n- compose/legacy/{conport-kg,leantime-overlay}-docker-compose.yml\n- docker/mcp-servers-source/{start-all-mcp-servers,start-profile,setup-task-orchestrator}.sh\n\nRuntime fixes required before these could safely go (discovered by tracing\nactual callers, not just grepping filenames):\n- src/dopemux/mcp/provision.py: MCPProvisioner used \"start-all-mcp-servers.sh\"\n  as its \"is this a valid MCP stack\" sentinel across every candidate source\n  (project local/source/vendor/cache/package template). Deleting the script\n  without changing this would have made `ensure_stack_present()` unlink the\n  docker/mcp-servers symlink and then raise, breaking `dopemux init`'s\n  MCP-provisioning flow. Swapped the sentinel to README.md, which ships with\n  every copy of the vendored tree and isn't a launch path.\n- src/dopemux/commands/mcp_commands.py: `dopemux mcp up` (no --repo) shelled\n  out to scripts/start-all-mcp-servers.sh directly for the --all/default\n  case. Replaced with the same docker-compose-service-list approach `mcp\n  down` already uses (DEFAULT_MCP_SERVICES ∩ compose services), so `dopemux\n  mcp up --all` — the command INSTALL.md now documents as canonical — no\n  longer depends on a script that doesn't exist.\n- .claude/hooks/mcp_health_probe.py: generic remediation suggestion changed\n  from `docker compose up -d {name}` to `dopemux mcp up --services {name}`.\n- .vibe/config.toml: task-orchestrator entry repointed from the FastAPI\n  shadow-twin at :8000 to the canonical Kotlin jar singleton at\n  127.0.0.1:7890/mcp (streamable HTTP), per design migration step M10.\n\nReference updates: INSTALL.md (drops the raw-script alternative at\n~L1157, extends the compose-deprecation note to cover the removed\ncompose/legacy/ files), scripts/README.md, docs/03-reference/services/\nserver-registry{,-2}.md and the vendored SERVER_REGISTRY.md copy (Quick\nReference now points at `dopemux mcp up --all`), and\nscripts/deploy/setup/install-mcp-servers.sh's closing hints.\n\nAdded tests/mcp/test_no_legacy_fleet_start_paths.py: a CI guard that walks\ngit-tracked executable files (*.sh/*.py/*.ps1/Makefile — prose in docs/JSON\ncan't launch anything) for `docker compose up` / `docker-compose up` and\nfails on any hit outside an explicitly justified allowlist. The sweep\nsurfaced two pre-existing, out-of-worklist direct-compose paths (Makefile's\npm-up/webhook_receiver targets, docker/leantime/configure_bridge.sh, and an\nunscoped scripts/deploy/setup/setup_dopemux.sh with no live caller) that are\nallowlisted with a note flagging them for a follow-up packet rather than\nrewritten here, to keep this change to the safe subset.\n\nUpdated tests/mcp/test_provision.py, tests/test_cli_mcp_startup.py, and\ntests/test_mcp_health_probe.py for the sentinel/suggestion-string changes\nabove.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"chore(mcp): remove legacy fleet launch paths (design P-22 safe subset)","oid":"b2f2f2d20f1d34dfdf150c7d049b87cf8493a248"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-28T23:22:24Z","authors":[{"email":"167156098+hu3mann@users.noreply.github.com","id":"U_kgDOCfaZgg","login":"hu3mann","name":"DDD-Enterprises (DJ Daddy Dom & the Department of… Don’t ask, Don’t tell, Don’t stop, Don’t you dare…)"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-28T23:22:24Z","messageBody":"…n (P-23 safe subset)\n\nAligns agent-facing rules and operator docs with\nclaudedocs/mcp-fleet-multi-instance-design-2026-07-28.md, building on the\nlegacy-script removal in b2f2f2d20f. Adds a sharing-class + command-surface\nsubsection to AGENTS.md §12 and a compact pointer in .claude/CLAUDE.md;\nreplaces the stale pre-#1052 port_allocator catch-22 workaround in\nmcp-integration-guide.md with the current identity-probe behavior; adds a\nDEPRECATED banner to instance-state-persistence.md for the superseded\nlettered A-E instance model; and sweeps live operator-facing docs (tutorials,\nhow-tos, current reference/explanation docs) to stop presenting port :8000 as\nthe task-orchestrator MCP (canonical is the Kotlin jar on :7890),\nregistry.yaml as the current MCP source of truth (superseded by\nmcp_catalog.yaml per ADR-MCPINT-001), or the lettered A-E instance model as\ncurrent outside the one file that documents it. Dated audit/research/history